+l_english:
+  gts_eromanga.name: "Best GTS Work of the Year"
+  gts_eromanga.1.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most prestigious entertainment awards—have been announced, with a simulation game titled §Y《Sky Blue Lane》§! taking the top prize. \nIn this game, players take on the role of a naval commander, leading massive shipgirls—measuring thousands of meters in length—into battle against equally massive Siren shipgirls. By skillfully balancing the expenditure of their shipgirls’ stamina with securing combat victories, players must protect both the harbor district and themselves from the threats posed by the shipgirls and the Sirens. \nSome believe this game directly influenced the Imperial Navy Department’s command training theories regarding space-based ship girls."
+  gts_eromanga.2.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most prestigious entertainment awards—have been announced, with a game titled §Y《Ark Knight》§! taking home the top prize. \nThis RPG creates a wondrous world, in which players take on the role of a research scientist at an observatory who makes an emergency landing on an indigenous world following a shuttle accident. Using their internal medical skills, players befriend and win over giant beast-girl operatives from various native races. After recruiting them into their ranks, players wage war across the land until the entire planet is subjugated under the rule of their giant feet. \nThe game has been widely praised for its art style and multiple endings, attracting many people to visit Terra—the planet that inspired the story—on pilgrimages. However, the planet is nowhere near as vibrant as it is in the story; it is now merely a rare crystal mining area for the Empire."
+  gts_eromanga.3.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most prestigious entertainment awards—have been announced, with a game titled §Y《Champion Derby》§! taking home the top prize. \nIn this casual simulation game, players take on the role of a rookie trainer managing a group of giant horse girls with distinct personalities. While training their various abilities, players must balance their relationships with each horse girl to ultimately lead them to victory in the galaxy’s most famous “Arima Memorial” Ideal City Destruction Race. \nBooming sales have prompted the game developer to announce that work on a sequel will begin shortly. In the sequel, players will be able to use consciousness-simulation devices to directly take on the role of a giant horse girl and experience the legendary Ideal City Destruction Race firsthand, or play as a Tiny person in Ideal City, struggling to survive under the giant hooves of the horse girls."
+  gts_eromanga.4.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most highly anticipated entertainment awards—have been announced, with an action game titled §Y《Futa/Grand Order》§! taking the top prize. \nSet in the distant 20th millennium, the Milky Way is invaded by a swarm from an extragalactic system. To combat this apocalyptic crisis, “Caldeum”—a secret Psionic Energy agency established by the Stellar Sea Community—appoints the Master (played by the player) to summon Giantess Heroic Spirits from various civilizations and time periods to battle the swarm. \nThe game’s boldest design feature is that when a Spirit is severely defeated by the swarm, she not only suffers clothing damage but also grows an extremely sensitive giant phallus. This not only affects her evasion and skill usage but also attracts monster attacks; she can only recover by promptly inserting the player into her urethra and having sex with other Spirits after she is removed from battle. This standout feature has propelled the game to viral fame, cementing its status as the Game of the Year. Industry experts predict that this title may become the most lucrative cash cow in the history of the §Y “Futa”§! series."
+  gts_eromanga.5.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most prestigious entertainment awards—have been announced, with a real-time strategy game titled §Y《Puppet Front》§! taking home the top prize. \nSet slightly earlier than its predecessor, the game follows the protagonist—an ordinary non-commissioned officer in the “Griffin” space mercenary corps—who is deployed to the war-torn ruins of the planet Vigilus. Players will command a group of giant mecha-Giantesses equipped with early-model thermal weapons to complete various missions assigned by their employer amidst the peril-filled wasteland: annihilating hostile forces, searching for valuable supplies, strengthening their team of giant mecha-Giantesses through repeated battles, building and expanding their base, and ultimately finding a way to escape this troubled land."
+  gts_eromanga.6.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most prestigious entertainment awards—have been announced, with a text-based dating simulation game titled §Y《Wind and Snow: The Forbidden Zone》§! taking home the top prize. \nIn this game, players take on the role of the Director of Security for the mega-corporation World Tree, commanding a group of “Apocalypse Girls”—young women who have been granted divine power and transformed into giant forms—to eliminate mutated creatures within contaminated zones, while deepening relationships with these Apocalypse Girls and forging romantic bonds during their adventure to save the world. \nThe game was developed by Ankasia Studio, a team long considered a “factory of trash,” but this title is surprisingly well-crafted. Aside from the fact that the game tends to steer players toward the personal route of a certain silver-haired, flat-chested Giantess—a common point of criticism—the game has almost no obvious flaws. The game features diverse and comprehensive routes and introduces innovations to traditional visual novel mechanics: after achieving a good ending with a single character, players can continue the game directly to pursue other characters who harbor feelings for them, until they reach the true ending where they marry all the Apocalypse Girls. Furthermore, the game features multiple realistic interactive scenarios for each romanceable character—such as beach vacations, erotic play, and wedding nights—allowing players to experience sweet moments with these Giantesses firsthand through consciousness integration."
+  gts_eromanga.7.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most prestigious entertainment awards—have been announced, with an RTS game titled §Y《Blue Files》§! taking the top prize. \nThe story is set in Kiwotos, a highly advanced academic metropolis, Players take on the role of the newly appointed advisor for the Chale Club, commanding gaming prodigy Midori Saiha, the Race Knight Momo Saiha, and other Giantess students from various schools to resolve crises both big and small. Through close interactions with them to build rapport, players gradually uncover the conspiracy lurking beneath this chaotic city. Defeat the evil dragon Yuka Hayase, who devours students’ money; the Great Demon Lord Rion Tsukizuki; and the mastermind behind all these sinister events—Hifumi Atsutani—who seeks to giantify herself to rule Kiwotos and monopolize all the Pelolo dolls. \nThis title has been widely acclaimed for its sophisticated RTS command mechanics and rich, relationship-driven storylines featuring Giantess schoolgirls. Although the game was censored and banned by the Millennium Academy Student Council due to sensitive content and inappropriate personal attacks—and the development team, “Game Development Club,” has since gone missing—it remains one of the most popular games of the year."
+  gts_eromanga.8.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most highly anticipated entertainment awards—have been announced, with a vehicle-based shooting game titled §Y《Girls und Panzer: Giantess O-Dō Fantasy Battle》§! taking first place. \nThis title continues the main storyline. The crew led by Miho Nishizumi—who gained the ability to grow to gigantic proportions after winning the previous National High School Tank Do Tournament—will use their own bodies as the battlefield in this installment, inviting teams from various high schools to compete in a friendly match inside their bodies. \nPlayers will control a tank crew from one of the many high schools featured in the original series, defeating other crews across multiple maps on the girls’ skin and inside their bodies, and then join four other qualifying crews to challenge the overall champion of the previous Tankery Championship—the super-giant Mihoshi Nishizumi and her four crew members. \nAs a fan-oriented game, this title has managed to break into the mainstream thanks to its highly authentic simulation of the body’s exterior and interior environments, as well as the sensation of trampling, achieving unexpected commercial success. In addition to the series’ traditional Story Mode and Versus Mode, this installment also introduced the Creative Workshop for the first time, allowing players to replace the final boss with other characters or attempt speed skating inside a girl’s O-channel while driving a battle tank. This high degree of freedom is a key reason for the game’s positive reception."
+  gts_eromanga.9.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most highly anticipated entertainment awards—have been announced, with a historical strategy game titled §Y《Europa Chronicles IV: Power-Enhanced Director’s Cut Definitive Edition》§! taking home the top prize. \nThis title takes the history of the Renaissance era on the planet Sol3 as its basis but reimagines it in a radically different way. It posits that on January 1, 1444, a meteor orbited Earth six times before crashing into Junburg, having first destroyed the stability of every nation and plunged the entire world into chaos. Energy from the Giantess within the meteorite leaked out and was absorbed by several beautiful young women from different nations, who rapidly grew into “Chosen Ones” standing thousands of meters tall and effortlessly seized control of their respective nations. Players take on the role of one of these Giantesses, leading their nation to conquer and expand across the land, defeating other Chosen Ones, teasing them until they blush, adding them to their harem, and leading the Giantesses to continue their conquest—ultimately turning the entire world into a chaotic mess. \nAlthough this work is often dismissed as a \"wank fest\" created by an author with a \"mind full of semen\" due to its overly explicit, unapologetic plot and massive amount of erotic CG, its explosive sales since release and consistently high number of concurrent online players have been more than enough to silence all doubters."
+  gts_eromanga.10.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most highly anticipated entertainment awards—have been announced, with a simulation game titled §Y《Frostpunk》§! taking home the top prize. \nSet in the late Industrial Revolution, the game follows the antics of two Celestial Giantesses whose playful brawl knocks the Empire’s homeworld off its orbital path. As the two depart the galaxy in high spirits, the survivors are left to struggle for survival amid a global blizzard. \nPlayers take on the role of a Royal Scientific Society commissioner called upon in a time of crisis to lead the “New London”—an early-model Giantess powered by coal for heating—and the thousands of refugees living aboard her, on a journey to the Empire’s northern frontier. Along the way, you’ll gather resources, upgrade equipment, and nurture the “New London’s” still-developing personality core, ultimately finding a new, habitable home for the Empire’s citizens. \nThe game has been widely praised for its unique art style and rich “raising a daughter” Experience. In subsequent DLCs, the development team has added other Giantesses and storylines: the composed and intellectual “Ark,” who bears the Imperial government’s final mission; the cheerful and passionate and who gets along well with the tiny people; the frail and often bullied “Winter Home”; and the “New Liverpool,” which starts from scratch with an uncertain future—among others. AI-themed merchandise based on these characters’ designs will also be released."
+  gts_eromanga.11.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most highly anticipated entertainment awards—have been announced, with a card battle game titled §Y《Asami’s Spire》§! taking home the top prize. \nThis title is the spiritual successor to the classic game §Y《Asami Tower》§! In it, players are Shrunk by an unknown magic and transported into senior student Asami Ba’s home. To find a way to return to their original size, players must enter through a hole in the stockings on her toes and climb upward through the pantyhose layer, the “double orifices” layer, and the “giant breasts” layer. They use cards to battle various enemies on Asami’s body, collect key fragments, and ultimately enter the final showdown at the indentation of her nipple to catch her attention. Additionally, the game features an \"Infinite Mode,\" where players are shrunk even further down to the size of a microorganism. They’ll battle new enemies during an even longer climb up the Asami Tower, experiencing in real time the immense impact of Asami’s daily routines on the outside world."
+  gts_eromanga.12.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most highly anticipated entertainment awards—have been announced, with an action-adventure game titled §Y《Eyjafjalla Ring》§! taking top honors. \nCelestial Leader Eyjafjalla removed the Toe Ring from her foot in the colony, preparing to take a long-awaited bath, completely unaware that the world within her Toe Ring had plunged into endless chaos as it gradually lost the nourishment of her body heat and foot sweat. Believing their goddess has abandoned them, the colonists rise in revolt; the Toe Ring United Government collapses with a crash, and a group of heroes, inspired by Psionic Energy revelations, begin vying for the goddess’s remaining bodily fluids. In this chaotic world, players will embark on a journey as the Faded One, crossing the Sea of Sweat and Mist, unifying the Toe Ring borderlands, and becoming the King of the Eyjafjalla Ring."
+  gts_eromanga.13.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most highly anticipated entertainment awards—have been announced, with a simulation management game titled §Y《Floating Ghost 2》§! taking the top prize. \nPicking up where the previous installment left off, players take on the role of a Giantess commander who, after successfully conquering the powerful “Habent United World”—a civilization of tiny people—will continue to oversee the occupation and reconstruction of the planet in this sequel. During the day, you’ll clear out unruly settlements of tiny persons, collect scientific and technological resources from the former government, and meet the production quotas set by the planetary governor—all while guarding against infiltration by the tiny person resistance, armed with advanced weaponry, into your office, bathroom, and bedroom. Strategically deploy your Giantess guards and Tiny person operatives to protect your rooms, raid Tiny person strongholds, and do your utmost to lower the room infiltration level—all to avoid being “trained” into a “Planetary Fury” for the Tiny person rebels.  nIn the new expansion §Y “Battle of the Apocalyptics”§!, enemy and friendly agent types have become more diverse, and the battlefield against Tiny person infiltration has expanded further. Players can command their loyal Tiny person agents from within the Giantess Commander’s shoes, socks, underwear, and even her body to engage in a life-and-death struggle against invading enemy forces."
+  gts_eromanga.14.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most prestigious entertainment awards—have been announced, with an RPG titled §Y《Giantess Creed: Black Flag》§! taking home the top prize. \nThe game is based on the life story of Arlo Kenway, a legendary Giantess pirate who once ruled the Star Sea Empire’s border star systems. Players will take on the role of this Giantess to experience the life of a 25th-century interstellar pirate. \nA young, unknown sailor named Arlo Kenway accidentally learns of the existence of a galactic relic—the Transcription Device—and, while searching for it, is arrested after discovering the Empire’s secret research into the Aether Phase Engine. After escaping captivity, Arlo and her companions seize a destroyer and name it the “Cold Raven” . She then befriends other renowned Giantess pirates of her era and embarks on a life of adventure, raiding Imperial treasure ships and hunting galactic behemoths. Ultimately, she breaks through the Imperial Royal Navy’s encirclement during a campaign against the Giantess pirates and establishes a free star sector on the edge of the galaxy, free from Imperial rule."
+  gts_eromanga.15.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most prestigious entertainment awards—have been announced, with a turn-based strategy game titled §Y《The Darkest Dungeon》§! taking home the top prize. The protagonist’s ancestor used dark magic to uncover the terrifying truth about this world—that the entire planet is nothing more than loose soil on the body of a Slumbering Celestial Giantess. The ancestor was struck by a fatal curse, and the entire family subsequently fell into decline. Players follow the ancestor’s dying wish to return to their homeland and save the family estate. \nPlayers must recruit mercenaries and use portals near the ancestral ruins to enter various parts of the Giantess’s body, where they’ll explore paths, collect treasures, and battle all manner of bizarre creatures mutated by her hormones. The long and arduous battles, the unsettling environment, and the vague sense of the truth will cause the mercenaries’ stress to mount, eventually leading to mental breakdowns and their decision to become part of this internal dungeon. After countless sacrifices and deaths, the player will lead the team to confront the deranged ancestor, put an end to her evil plan, and ensure that the Giantess’s slumber deep underground continues."
+  gts_eromanga.16.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most prestigious entertainment awards—have been announced, with a title titled §Y《Xiao Ye Company》§! taking home the top prize. \nThis historical simulation management game faithfully recreates the arduous journey of the Tiny Person civilization as they first discovered and began to utilize the bodily fluids of the Giantesses. Players take on the role of a tiny person manager who, with the help of AI characters like Angelina and others, receives and cares for Giantesses from other races sent by headquarters. They must direct employees to stimulate the Giantesses into secreting bodily fluids through communication, intimate contact, maintenance and cleaning, and even threats and intimidation. While meeting production quotas, players must also stabilize the emotions of the housed Giantesses to prevent them from losing control and escaping, which could lead to unforeseeable disasters."
+  gts_eromanga.17.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most highly anticipated entertainment awards—have been announced, with an action game titled §Y《Black-Fur Cat: Pulu》§! taking home the top prize. \nThis work imagines an alternate ending to the Battle of Heaven: After the legendary cat-girl warrior Apro led her forces to defeat the two Awakened Empires, she intended to retire and spend the rest of her life on an ordinary planet inhabited by Tiny persons. However, she was tragically betrayed by the Fourth Calamity; the Tiny persons she had raised were seized as playthings by other Giantess leaders, and Apro is beaten to death by her former comrade, Yanqi Repu. Players will take on the role of the Hakki—heirs to the Will of the Keycaps who emerge out of nowhere centuries later. To uncover the truth behind the “Supermarket Mystery” surrounding Apro, they will battle Giantess leaders of all sizes and ultimately fulfill their destiny to become the strongest and most ruthless Giantess."
+  gts_eromanga.18.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most prestigious entertainment awards—have been announced, with a first-person shooter (FPS) game titled §Y《Field War 1》§! taking top honors. \nSet against the backdrop of the First Earth United Civil War, the game allows players to experience firsthand a series of conflicts and campaigns across Earth’s vast battlefronts between the two hegemonic blocs: the Entente and the Allies. To simulate an era of explosive military technological advancement—when giant mecha evolved from cutting-edge industrial marvels into mass-produced war machines—the game creatively introduces the “Giantess” mechanic. When one side falls behind, a Giantess arrives to provide support; these hundreds-of-meters-tall Giantesses can effortlessly tip the Libra of war: “Zeppelin” can crush the Graba Mountain Tunnel with a single stomp and grind most of a banquet hall to dust beneath her breasts with a single tumble; “Dreadnought” can ram through the century-old fortress of Faou, and shatter the coastal defenses of Zeebrugge; “Char” watches over the highlands of Soissons, and once corrupted, can level the supposedly impregnable Fort Faulx with a single kick; “Odin” and “Zamurets” rampage through the sandy deserts of the Middle East and the snowy plains of Eastern Europe. Yet the Giantesses of this era are not invincible; enemy soldiers can use various explosives and artillery to try to blow their outfits off, ultimately forcing them into a state of embarrassment and causing them to faint on the ground. \nThe First Earth United Civil War concluded with “Zeppelin” storming Paris and Britain’s conditional surrender, bringing thirty years of peace to the Allied Powers (later known as the Imperial Covenant). Thirty years later, the Imperial Covenant would face its second decisive battle against the Industrial Union in the West and the Lucia Alliance in the East."
+  gts_eromanga.19.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most highly anticipated entertainment awards—have been announced, with a casual game titled §Y《Tales of Starlight Grains》§! taking home the top prize. \nAfter being laid off by the corporate giant Joja, players return to their hometown of Wenko Water, a Gaia-like planet meticulously transformed by horticultural automatons, to stay with their Giantess older sister, who runs a farm. In addition to farming and raising livestock in the bonsai garden their sister has prepared for them, players will also leverage their advantage as a Tiny person on this planet full of Giantesses, venturing into mines inaccessible to the Giantesses to explore, collect various ancient treasures, help the townspeople resist the Enterprise’s economic infiltration, interact with various Giantesses as the seasons change, and ultimately forge friendships or even marital relationships. \nThe game’s careful attention to mechanics, music, and atmosphere perfectly fulfills players’ fantasies of living in harmony with Giantesses in an idyllic pastoral setting, creating a virtual haven filled with warmth and the joy of exploration for the Tiny persons who are often toyed with by the Giantesses."
+  gts_eromanga.20.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most prestigious entertainment awards—have been announced, with a real-time strategy game titled §Y *Command & Conquer: Mind Omega* §! taking top honors. \nThis title serves as a narrative expansion of its predecessor, §Y《Command & Conquer: Yuri’s Revenge》§!, allowing players to experience a timeline entirely distinct from the original through a series of campaigns commanding three factions: Following the First Soviet-Moe War, the New Soviet Union—backed by the Moe Army—lay low with the help of Yuri, a yuri Giantess enthusiast, before launching a surprise attack that dealt a crushing blow to the Moe Army, sparking the Second Soviet-Moe War. As the war progressed, Yuri attempted to reap the benefits as a third party, and his conspiracy to establish a world ruled by Giantesses came to light, forcing the Soviet Union and the Moe Army to temporarily cooperate and jointly eliminate Yuri’s Epsilon Legion. \nAlthough the Soviet-Moe Alliance successfully recaptured most of the territory occupied by the Epsilon Legion, they failed to prevent Libra—a super-powered Giantess bred by Yuri—from activating the mind-control tower during the Antarctic Campaign. Ultimately, Libra took control of all human minds and grew into a 10,000-meter-tall Giantess, ushering in a new era for Earth’s civilization. \nThe only hope for ending this catastrophe rested with the newly formed Fengfeng faction. Through reverse engineering, Yunru—who had also grown into a 10,000-meter-tall Giantess—led exiled forces from various nations to establish a containment barrier at Cape Hope in Alaska, awaiting the opportunity to resist Libra."
