+  gts_hitomi.30001.desc: "An unfamiliar communication signal was directly routed to our main channel. \nShe identified herself as “Hitomi Mitsuki,” a freelancer who has long operated between the border and unregistered sectors, taking on various assignments. \nShe submitted a short-term employment application to us with a clearly defined timeframe. According to the contract, during her employment, she will serve us as a scientist, participating in scientific research, investigations, and the analysis of special projects. It should be noted that once the agreement takes effect, the ship equipment and fleet command interface she currently displays will not be transferred to our system as part of the employment. In this collaboration, she will join our operational sequence as a “researcher” rather than a “commander.” \nAt the end of the communication, she raised her eyes slightly, her tone so calm it bordered on matter-of-fact:\n“Don’t give me that look. You’re hiring my knowledge, experience, and judgment—not this stuff.”"
+  gts_hitomi.30001.a: "Really... really?!"
+  gts_hitomi.30002.desc: "You, you, you, you… What are you staring at?! Hey! That kind of stare is so rude! I’m just here to be a scientist, not to be your exhibit… And don’t touch my ears!\nOh, right, here’s a little gift for you—make sure to thank me properly, okay?~"
