+  gts_hitomi.30005.desc: "That day, Hitomi Mitsuki was sitting in front of her terminal, intently processing a mountain of scientific and archaeological data. Her fingers flew across the control panel; she was so focused that there was hardly a single superfluous movement, except for those fluffy ears standing up among her hair, which would occasionally twitch slightly in response to her thoughts or emotional fluctuations. \nYour gaze soon found itself drawn there involuntarily.\nSoft, fluffy, and moving.\nIt was simply impossible not to notice them…\nFaced with ears so close at hand and completely unguarded, could you really resist reaching out to touch them?"
+  gts_hitomi.30005.a: "How could I possibly resist that! Grab her hard!"
+  gts_hitomi.30006.desc: "“That’s very rude of you.”\nHitomi Mitsuki tilted her head slightly, a faint, almost imperceptible smile playing at the corners of her lips, but her eyes clearly no longer held the casual composure she’d feigned just moments ago. \n“Rude little bugs like you… are going to be punished, you know~”\nIn the next instant, the light streaming through the window was suddenly blocked. \nAccompanied by a heart-stopping tremor, Hitomi Mitsuki’s form rapidly expanded outside the building, swelling to a hundred times its original size in the blink of an eye. Her colossal figure stood towering between the skyscrapers, as if the entire city were nothing more than a model she could casually toy with at her feet. She leaned forward slightly, gazing down through the exterior walls and window panes at the tiny figures below—who had fallen into chaos at the sight of her—with a touch of mockery and a sense of condescending composure.\nThe once-bright office suddenly went dark. You braced yourself against the desk and inched your way toward the window. The next second, an eye so enormous it made your scalp tingle appeared on the outside of the glass, nearly filling the entire window. The eye curved slightly, a hint of amusement in its gaze, as if admiring the tiny figure frozen in fear behind the glass. \nImmediately afterward, a deafening roar swept in from outside the building, making even the air seem to tremble at the sound of her voice.\n“What’s the matter?” She blinked, her voice still carrying that lighthearted tone that made your scalp prickle. “Weren’t you so brave just a moment ago? Now you can’t even stand up straight?”\nYou opened your mouth, but not a single word came out. Reason couldn’t possibly explain what was happening before your eyes; your instinct left you with only one thought—run. \n“Tsk, how petty,” Hitomi puffed out her cheeks slightly, her tone tinged with displeasure, yet sounding as if she were deliberately teasing her prey. “Since no one’s willing to admit their mistake, I’ll just have to dish out a little punishment myself, then~” n“Gotcha,” she said softly, her ears twitching with delight. “So, you rude little thing—what kind of punishment do you think you deserve?” nThe perspective gradually shifted upward, and his field of vision was slowly filled by the ample bosom of the giant cat-girl before him—the first thing to catch his eye was the thin blue bustier covering her chest and the white fabric that barely concealed her cleavage, followed by the cleavage that constantly exuded a faint milky scent. She tilted her palm slightly, and the little fellow in her hand was tucked into the “canyon” below, positioned just right to give him a clear, bird’s-eye view of the entire city spread out beneath him. \n“Just stay right here and watch carefully,” Hitomi said, tilting her head with a smile so sweet it sent a chill down his spine. “Watch as I destroy your country, your city, and those subjects of yours who think they’re so useful.” n Hitomi crouched slightly; the shadow cast by her body gradually engulfed the stream of traffic below. Some people, swept up in the torrent, frantically got out of their cars to flee, only to suddenly realize that the surrounding roads had been completely blocked off. \nBut Hitomi paid no heed to those struggling for their lives. She extended her fingertip and crushed the tiny persons on her shoe—with just a light press, the persons that had been wriggling on the shoe’s surface turned into a viscous pulp, clinging to her fingertip and the shoe’s surface as thin threads of goo stretched between them. \nThe previously restless crowd suddenly fell silent. Just a few seconds later, the silent crowd immediately scattered in all directions, but people were fleeing in different directions, pushing and shoving one another in an attempt to carve out a path to safety. Yet this chaotic stampede clearly offered no effective means of escape; one living being after another vanished beneath Hitomi’s sneakers, wiped out beneath her fingertips…\n“Hmm…?” nThe cat ears on her head twitched slightly as she caught the sound of an engine. She looked in the direction of the noise and saw a reckless sports car roaring past her feet. But for a cat girl of such imposing stature, moving at such high speed right in front of her was clearly unwise.\n“Little one, where are you running off to?” nThe girl slowly stood up, stretched lazily, and then took a gentle step forward—her towering sneakers blocked her path like a blue-and-white wall, and the sports car slammed into them before it could even hit the brakes. \n“Gotcha. So...”\nThe violent impact nearly knocked the tiny person in the driver’s seat unconscious; if his beloved car hadn’t been equipped with airbags, he would have lost his life right then and there. \nWhen he opened his eyes again, the wall that had nearly cost him his life was standing upright —Hitomi had her foot raised halfway; the soles of her sneakers were caked with road debris, vehicle wreckage, and human flesh and blood, yet even so, the shoes still looked brand-new. Just by looking at them, it was clear their owner didn’t wear them very often. \nThe tread patterns on the soles were imprinted with cute little cat symbols, and paired with the tiny size tag, they looked, no matter how you looked at them, like a pair of adorable sneakers perfect for a young girl—they’d even be just right for his little daughter…\nCreak— nAs Hitomi’s sole slowly pressed down, the sports car’s frame began to twist and deform, unable to withstand such immense force. The entire car—along with the Tiny person inside—was crushed by Hitomi’s sole into a mangled sheet of metal stamped with cute patterns; from any angle, it was impossible to recognize its original form. No matter how expensive or eye-catching this sports car had once been, it had now become a thin sheet of metal, stuck to Hitomi’s sole and firmly wedged into the tread grooves.\n“How pathetic. Even a toy kitten is sturdier than your little car.” ”\nHitomi slowly curled her foot backward. The little car—now completely molded to the shape of her sole—and its poor owner inside clung to her shoe with reluctance, though that was only from her perspective.\n “No matter how much you don’t want to, you’ll have to get off my sole~”\nShe gave her foot a gentle shake, and the wreckage of the car on her sole fell off like trash that had been stepped on, then plummeted to the ground, where it lay sprawled in a twisted, mangled heap. \nJust as she wiggled her foot, a bus packed with passengers was racing through the city at top speed, trying to escape this disaster-stricken area while she wasn’t looking. \nUnfortunately, prey rarely manages to escape from under a cat girl’s watchful eye.\n“Oh my, a little guy has come right to me~”\nHitomi leaned forward slightly and grabbed the bus that was trying to escape from the side of her foot, as effortlessly as a house cat catching a mouse. \nAs for the passengers inside, all they saw was their bus suddenly coming to a halt just as it was about to escape the most dangerous area. At the same time, several enormous fingers appeared outside the windows, then lifted the bus up until it was right in front of the giant cat girl who was having a field day in the city. \n“It’s packed! Looks like the little ones really enjoy this cramped feeling~?”"
+  gts_hitomi.30006.a: "Fortunately, the loss wasn't too great."
+  gts_hitomi.30007.desc: "In fact, most of the passengers on this packed bus were commuters rushing to catch the early shift; if their financial situation and time constraints hadn’t left them with no other choice, they wouldn’t have wanted to sit on such a crowded bus. \n“I’ve come up with a fun little game… You’d all love to be toyed with like that, wouldn’t you~?”\nBut she didn’t give the tiny people inside a chance to answer. Instead, she pressed both hands against the top and bottom of the bus and gradually squeezed inward…\n“Hurry up and open the doors for me!” \nUnder threat from several angry passengers, the driver opened the door, but the moment they saw the scene outside, they trembled and retreated back inside. \nWhat they saw was a hand of enormous proportions—the likes of which they’d never seen in their lives—and beneath that hand was a drop of at least a hundred meters, with the familiar city streets only visible far below.\n“Why come back? Run! If you’re not going to escape, I’m getting out of here first.” nAn unsuspecting passenger, mocking the retreating group, walked toward the door and then vanished from the others’ sight.  nHis body plummeted toward the ground, crashing heavily onto an unoccupied car at Hitomi’s feet. The impact instantly mangled his form beyond recognition, reducing him to a pulpy, blood-soaked mess. \n\n“Hitomi’s homemade cat treats—just thinking about them makes my mouth water~”\nHer palm gradually closed. First, the edges of her palm slowly sealed together, burying the light streaming into the car—along with the passengers’ last glimmer of hope for survival. \nA sticky sensation gradually spread across the palm of Hitomi's hand. Hitomi carefully sensed the process of life fading away, feeling the sensation of an entire busload of people being gradually ground to a pulp by her own hands. \n“I think that’s about right…”\nShe moved one hand aside, allowing the outside light to once again flood this pitiful bus. It was just a pity that not a single living soul remained inside, and the vehicle had been reduced to a flattened hunk of metal coated with a bit of meat paste. \n“Let me see how these little guys taste~”\nHitomi opened her mouth slightly and gently took a bite of the steel cat stick, which reeked of blood. Her fingers gently pinched the tail end of the “cat stick” and slowly pushed it forward— nShe gently licked the meat paste continuously oozing from the “cat treat’s” opening with the tip of her tongue, savoring the “exquisite” flavor of this paste—a blend of the lives of dozens of people—filled with the pungent smell of blood and a fresh, sweet taste that only she could perceive. \n“So delicious~ Ah—huh? It’s already gone? These tiny people really don’t last long.” nJust as Hitomi was about to continue enjoying her special cat treat, she suddenly realized that this cat treat, made by Tiny people, wasn’t nearly as substantial as a normal one; she’d only just had a taste before it was completely gone. \nHitomi’s tongue forcefully pried open the bus, which had been crushed flat like a sheet of iron. She licked and probed inside, trying to scoop up any remaining meat sauce, until she could find nothing more. Only then, with a heavy heart, did she roll the “cat treat shell” into a small metal ball and popped it into her mouth like a candy bean. \n“This little guy’s bus doesn’t taste all that great either… Well, I guess I’ve had a bit of breakfast, at least.  nImmediately afterward, the rest of the city didn’t escape unscathed either; under her casual trampling and tampering, it was successively reduced to a shambles.”\nIn this bustling city, she couldn’t see a single building taller than she was; even in the busiest downtown area, she couldn’t find a single structure that towered above her. Given her current size, she could easily treat the entire city as her very own playground. \n“What a bunch of nobodies. Such a huge city, and not a single building taller than me. How boring—” n Hitomi’s figure gradually vanished into the fog, which had suddenly thickened. By the time the fog cleared, the section of the city where the enormous cat girl had stood was left with nothing but a barren patch of earth-brown land and a colossal paw print shaped like a ball of cat paws. \nAt least for the humans in this city, the danger had temporarily vanished."
+  gts_hitomi.30008.desc: "Hitomi Mitsuki’s temporary employment agreement has reached its scheduled termination date. \nIn accordance with the terms of the originally registered contract, her temporary staff privileges in our database, her access permissions to research terminals, and her project assistance privileges will all be revoked as of today. The final research report has been neatly filed, and she has even taken the initiative to highlight any anomalous data requiring follow-up in the appendix. \nThe communication channel fell silent for a few seconds.\nOn the screen, Hitomi Mitsuki didn’t leave immediately. She simply crossed her arms, as if she had long anticipated this moment, yet seemed somewhat displeased by our silence.\n“...It’s time, isn’t it.” n She blinked gently, her tone still calm, though a touch softer than usual.\n“Don’t give me that look. A contract is a contract, and I’m a woman of my word. I’ve done everything I was supposed to do, and I’ve left you all the necessary data. From here on out, even without me, you should be able to handle things just fine, right?”\nShe raised her hand and tapped the small terminal beside her; the signal, which had been maintaining a shallow connection, began to gradually fade.\n“But then again… if there really is something you absolutely need me for, go take a look at that little gift I left behind.” nJust before the connection was about to cut off, she turned her head as if to add one last thing.\n“Oh, and don’t say I left too suddenly. I already told you all this fifteen years ago.”\nThen, the signal fell silent.\nHitomi Mitsuki has terminated her temporary employment contract and left our service roster."
+  gts_hitomi.30008.a: "We will remember this collaboration."
+  gts_hitomi.30008.a_custom: "(Hitomi Mitsuki left our party in March. \nYou can continue to trigger subsequent special events through the “Hitomi Mitsuki’s Chibi Figure.”)"
+  gts_hitomi.30009.desc: "After we manually activated the “Chibi Figure of Hitomi Mitsuki,” this small device—which appeared to be nothing more than a souvenir—suddenly ceased all normal responses. \nA few seconds later, a faint blue-white glow shone from the figurine’s eyes. The emergency subroutine hidden within was fully activated, and a set of coordinates never recorded on our star charts was projected onto the center of the bridge. \nThese coordinates lay outside known navigation routes. \nA voice—familiar yet utterly unfamiliar—echoed through the communication channel.\n“Target confirmed.”\n“Civilization ID: Connected.”\n“Observation variables: Will, Adaptability, Combat Endurance.” n“Tester: Hitomi Mitsuki.”\nAfter a brief silence, the voice continued:\n“This is the initial test.”\n“And it is also the final test.”\nNew navigation targets popped up simultaneously on every terminal in the bridge.\nAn unknown galaxy appeared at the edge of our star map."
+  gts_hitomi.30009.a: "Analyze these coordinates."
+  gts_hitomi.30011.desc: "When our fleet arrived at the target coordinates, a dense fleet was already waiting. All the ships were arranged in an extremely precise formation, like the limbs of some vast consciousness. Then, a holographic projection spanning the stellar orbits lit up at the center of the galaxy. \nHitomi Mitsuki appeared there. \nHer figure was magnified to near-celestial proportions; her white-and-blue attire was covered in mechanized armor, and her cat ears and tail had been reconstructed from high-dimensional light bands and metallic structures. She hovered silently at the center of the galaxy, her eyes cast downward as she looked down upon our fleet. \nBefore her, even battleships appeared no more than tiny specks of light floating at the edge of her palm.\nShe slowly raised her hand.\nThe unmanned fleet within the galaxy sprang into action, their engines glowing as brightly as the Stars.\n“Conclusion: The test may begin.” n“I am Hitomi Mitsuki.”\n“The Heartless Cat.”\nHer gaze fell upon our flagship. In that instant, everyone on the bridge experienced an illusion: it wasn’t that we were entering this galaxy, but that the entire fleet had been placed by her into some precision laboratory vessel. \n“Come on, little civilization.”\n“Prove that you’re still worth recording.”"
+  gts_hitomi.30011.a: "Entire fleet, stand by for combat."
+  gts_hitomi.30012.desc: "The last reconnaissance fleet disintegrated under our fire. Within the spacetime rift, the fleet’s once-precise formation began to fade layer by layer. Those lifeless combat units transformed into countless blue-and-white specks of light, flowing against the current along the galaxy’s orbit, and ultimately merging into the massive projection of Hitomi Mitsuki. \nShe lowered her gaze, quietly watching our fleet. \nIn the next instant, Hitomi Mitsuki’s projection began to gradually solidify. In its place appeared the familiar blue-and-white figure we once knew. At that moment, Hitomi Mitsuki was so immense that the fleet seemed to hover like dust before her fingertips.\n“Incorporate the traits of the weak humans to pursue true power.”"
+  gts_hitomi.30012.a: "Let's get started"
+  gts_hitomi.30013.desc: "After Hitomi Mitsuki’s body was pierced at its final anchor point, it finally ceased moving. The stellar trajectory spanning the spacetime rift fractured layer by layer, and the bands of light that had once sealed off the battlefield disintegrated into countless blue-and-white shards before our fleet, slowly scattering like a nebula that had lost its heat; She lowered her eyes, the light in her pupils flickering incessantly. All that remained on the communication channel was intermittent, icy static: “Assessment… mimicking the posture and movements of tiny persons… has no effective impact on combat capability… severe damage… System shutting down…” After a brief silence, she seemed to still want to raise her hand to continue fighting, but that enormous hand—large enough to obscure the entire fleet—merely trembled slightly before disintegrating into specks of light in front of the flagship. “Cannot accept… failure… hardware… has exceeded endurance limits…” Her voice grew fainter and fainter, yet it seemed as though she were stubbornly repeating something: “Even so… I must grow stronger… Even so… I must press on… Become even stronger… Keep moving forward…” Before the last glimmer of light faded from her eyes, Hitomi Mitsuki looked toward our fleet, yet it was as if she were gazing toward an even more distant horizon, “Stronger… farther… I want to witness… the end of endless evolution…” The communication cut off, the massive projection vanished completely, and everything within the spacetime rift fell into silence."
+  gts_hitomi.30013.a: "Is it over?"
+  gts_hitomi.30014.desc: "Just as our fleet was about to declare the battle over, a strange yet gentle voice suddenly emerged from the depths of the silence, A new figure appeared at the center of the shattered stellar trail. She had ears and a silhouette similar to March’s, yet wore simpler, more modest attire; her violet eyes gazed quietly at the specks of light scattered across the void; She did not look toward our fleet, but instead walked slowly toward the spot where Hitomi Mitsuki had vanished, as if calling out to a creation she had fashioned with her own hands, yet which had been lost for far too long: “…March.” ” The shards responded to her; faint glimmers coalesced once more. The slumbering Mizuki Hitomi seemed to hear something, her fragmented consciousness echoing intermittently through the void: “Mitsuki… why have you come here?” Mizuki Hitomi gently raised her hand, cradling a tiny speck of light in her palm, and gently pressed it against March’s chest. In the next instant, both of their figures lit up simultaneously. The once-silent rift in space-time was reignited by a blue-white glow, and the shards scattered all around, as if answering a call, began to converge on them one by one. Just then, Mizuki Hitomi suddenly turned her head to glance at us and even blinked quite naturally. Although she didn’t say a word, that expression looked exactly like she was saying, “Don’t celebrate just yet—I’ll beat you all to tears in a second.jpg.” ” Before the bridge crew could even react, the silence was completely shattered. Countless points of light coalesced once more within the rift in space-time, and Hitomi Mitsuki’s figure reappeared amidst the radiance."
+  gts_hitomi.30014.a: "That doesn't seem right."
+  gts_hitomi.30015.desc: "Hitomi Mitsuki stood at the center of the galaxy. She was silent for a long time before saying softly, “Even if I obtain that unknown power, I still won’t be able to avoid the end, will I…” Hitomi Mitsuki looked at Mizuki Hitomi, her ears twitching slightly as if she were thinking deeply for a few seconds: “…Are you saying we should keep moving forward with them?” Hitomi Mitsuki was silent for a moment, then seemed to finally accept this answer—which sounded a bit strange, but wasn’t unpleasant: “I understand. I’ll take your advice this time.” She turned and looked at our fleet: “Thank you for your assistance with the scan. Seeing you give it your all has opened up entirely new possibilities for me.” She raised her hand slightly, and the specks of light scattered throughout the rift in space-time gathered, coalescing into a new identity beacon that slowly settled into our database. “This world has taught me a great deal. From here on, I will set out on a journey to continue learning about this world, documenting it—and moving forward alongside you all.” ” Mizuki Hitomi added quietly from the side: “In other words, she’s officially joining the team.” Hitomi Mitsuki’s cheeks flushed slightly, but she didn’t argue; she simply nodded gently: “…Yes. I look forward to working with you all from now on.”"
+  gts_hitomi.30015.a: "Welcome back, Hitomi Mitsuki."
+  gts_hitomi.30016.name: "No-effect events"
+  gts_hitomi.30016.desc: "I guess it's a souvenir now?"
+  gts_hitomi.30016.a: "Not under construction"
+  gts_hitomi.30017.desc: "This—this time, I’m not just here on a whim… Seeing you all give it your all has shown me new possibilities, so I’m officially joining you. I’ll keep learning about this world and documenting it, and while I’m at it, I’ll take care of all those troublesome research projects—but, but don’t think this means you can just stare at me whenever you want. And you still can’t touch my ears!"
