+  gts_ora.100.a.desc: "Hello... There's no need to be so formal; we could use a more casual way of addressing each other..."
+  gts_ora.10.a: "I'd like to hear your story"
+  gts_ora.101.desc: "“A story, you say…? I’d be happy to.”\nThe girl turned the page.\n“It’s all right here. What would you like to hear?”"
+  gts_ora.10.a.custom: "You can use the following three options to exchange Imperial population for basic resources."
+  gts_ora.101.a: "\"The Dream Realm of Forgotten Illusions\""
+  gts_ora.101.a.custom: "Consume people to earn energy coins"
+  gts_ora.101.a.response: "“A young girl had a dream of an ideal realm sprinkled with powdered sugar. In her dream, she met the gentlest of girls—who seemed like the perfect playmate, and perhaps even a family member for eternity. They were so close that even if she were to be eaten, she would do so willingly; it seemed as though this was part of that tenderness, causing all untimely memories to fade away. ”\n“The future is the future of the past, yet the past is an existence the future has long since abandoned. In the realm of dreams, the girl closes the loop between her past and future, for only in dreams can she reveal her most vulnerable side.”\nSleep well. May you encounter a gentle Giantess like Bai An in your dreams—I promise. \n\nThe story ends with the girl’s words, but upon receiving it, she decides to trade a few small resources with you for a little… “snack”?\n(You traded 2,500 Energy Coins to Ora for a population boost.)"
+  gts_ora.101.b: "*Redemption at the End of the Stars*"
+  gts_ora.101.b.custom: "Use people to obtain minerals"
+  gts_ora.101.b.response: "A tiny person once found herself trapped in this cycle of self-justification. She chased after the Giantess’s footsteps along the cracks in the floor tiles, yet throughout her entire life, she was never able to get even a single step closer to the Giantess. \nShe had lost hope; she had been mired in a quagmire; she had distrusted fate; and she had been pushed into the abyss by those with ulterior motives. Unlike the protagonists in other tales, she possessed no flashy powers. For someone like her, even attempting to challenge the gods was utterly impossible. \nFortunately, she was not a lone star burning out; she had companions who journeyed alongside her, granting her once again the right to stand against the gods. The Tiny person held a long umbrella, like a hero’s sword, and her faith became her only magic.\nBut then again, you’re not a lone star either, are you? You have the Giantess you met along the way… and me. \n\nThe story ends with the girl’s words, but upon receiving it, she decides to trade a few small resources with you in exchange for a little… “snack”? \n(You traded 2,500 minerals to Ora for population.)"
+  gts_ora.101.c: "\"A Choice Beneath the Xuanxing Tower\""
+  gts_ora.101.c.custom: "Consume people to obtain food"
+  gts_ora.101.c.response: "“Compromise” or “resistance”—this has always been the question. \nXing has always believed that he shouldn’t rely on Xuan, the “culprit” who toppled the tower. He hates the tower; what he hates is the “cannibalistic” situation in this society of Tiny persons, which is as ruthless as a death line. Yet this outward resistance to Xuan, the Giantess, is actually a “compromise” with his current life.\nXuan’s upbringing, however, taught her that Tiny persons should be given the right to choose—not for any other reason, but out of her own “sense of righteousness”—the justification for bringing them back. It was a form of “gentleness,” yet it was a “compromise” toward the Tiny persons. \nAs for Xiao Ta, he had compromised too much; the collapse of the tower had once left him on the brink of being “executed.” And he understood one truth very clearly: Xing’s “resistance” could not last long. Since following Xuan offered him a chance at survival—and he was already considered “dead” by the society of Tiny persons—his goal was to free Xing from the heavy burdens of life and lead him into the Giantess’s embrace. \nHowever, in the end, the Giantess toppled the tower of prejudice—an ending everyone wanted to see. As for you, rest assured: with me here, we won’t choose to “compromise” on our future, will we? \n\nThe story ends with the girl’s words, but as she receives the story, she decides to use a few small resources to trade with you for a little… “snack”?\n(You used population points to trade with Ora for 2,500 food.)"
+  gts_ora.10.b: "Hurry up and use your \"Queen of All Women\" charm to figure something out!"
