+  councilor_gts_ora: "Giantess Ambassador"
+  councilor_gts_ora_desc: "Although everyone thought it was only natural for Ora to bear such a title, as far as she was concerned… Ora simply said, “Do as you please,” and gently pushed all the Tiny people who had come seeking her fame out with her shoe."
+  gts_ora.1001.name: "“I’m sorry… but I think I have to go.”"
+  gts_ora.1001.desc: "After Ora joined the Empire, her exceptional management skills and approachable nature quickly brought the entire empire under orderly governance. Although she was the size of a celestial body, her body could sometimes span an entire celestial body or even a galaxy. Under her leadership, no one dared to act with impunity anymore. However, the budget allocated to Ora’s lifestyle was actually less than that of some average-sized Giantesses. Aside from her ability to freely alter her size, her generally simple and unassuming lifestyle might also be a contributing factor. \nYes, it’s hard to imagine finding a Giantess in this vast sea of stars who is so idealistic—one who rarely even takes the life of a Tiny person. However, compared to those Giantesses who can destroy an entire planet at the drop of a hat, even Ora—despite being a Celestial Giantess—merely “eats” a few Tiny persons when carrying out punishments. However… although the tiny people she devours never emerge from Ora’s body again, as the only group that might ever come out of her stomach, you know just how terrifying it must be in there. \nAlthough Ora is merely a civil official and doesn’t possess the formidable military capabilities of other Giantesses, her body more than makes up for it—we should be grateful that a large portion of the law enforcement budget was saved and redirected toward covering the daily expenses of the other Giantesses. After all… on a planet governed by Ora, any criminal would likely end up in her stomach. \nHowever… this situation didn’t last long. Five years later, as you looked at her expired contract and received her message, you knew it was time for her to leave. \n“I’m sorry… but I might have to leave.”\nThe confines of the system may not be able to restrain this bird in flight, but the destination she’s flying toward is the long, dark night. After the young woman hands you her resignation letter, one thing becomes crystal clear: you can’t see her smile, nor can you see her usual lightheartedness. Just as you were about to ask something, your finger was pressed against by hers—a gesture telling you to say no more, or perhaps… urging you to say something."
+  gts_ora.1001.a: "“Before I leave… let me hold this one last time.”"
+  gts_ora.1001.a.custom: "§H “Don’t worry—parting is just so we can meet again under better circumstances. I hope that by then… you’ll see a more ‘mature’ me~”§!"
+  gts_ora.1001.b: "\"...I am not accepting your resignation.\""
+  gts_ora.1001.b.custom: "Ora will remain in the Empire\n(Stay tuned for content in future updates)"
+  gts_ora.1002.desc: "\"Okay, then please snuggle up closer.\"\nThe entire planet was cradled within Ora’s body, and the girl gently held this fragile life in her arms—the planet was beautiful, yet fragile.\nYou didn’t know what Ora was going to do, nor did you know where she would go after she left. You have even less idea whether Ora will ever return, or when you’ll see her again. In any case, the young girl packed her belongings and left this place, but she left something behind:\nA planet—the so-called “Lone Star Prison”—she entrusted this star system to you. Perhaps… does this mean she’ll come back?\nBut when you returned to your office, you saw that an elegant notebook had been left on your desk. You recognized it—it was something Ora had always carried with her. Now that it was sitting on your desk, presumably this was also something she had left for you. Just as you were about to open the first page, you noticed a note stuck to the cover:\n“Don’t worry. We’ll meet again someday.”"
