+  gts_ora.1003.desc: "“Huh? Is that so?”\nYou could see a flash of surprise in the girl’s eyes, but in the blink of an eye, she was back to her usual cheerful self.\n “Sigh. Someday, I’ll cram all your crimes—including, but not limited to, child labor, wage theft, and forced labor—into this little notebook… But until then, I’m going to keep a close eye on you.”\nWell, in any case, you’ve managed to keep this celestial-level administrator within the empire. But… you’ve unwittingly stumbled into a situation with no turning back. Still, on the bright side, at the very least, being under the protection of a Celestial Giantess… and perhaps even getting closer to her—no matter how you look at it, that doesn’t seem like a bad thing, does it?"
+  gts_ora.1004.desc: "“Don’t worry—I’ll still be waiting for you at the end of time.”"
+  gts_ora.1005.desc: "Time flies by so quickly, as if you can’t even catch a glimpse of it; in the blink of an eye, your empire seems to have entered its next phase.\nDuring this time, you’ve experienced a great deal and lost a great deal as well, but fortunately, what you’ve gained has always been deeply meaningful. Yet… on a day as calm as any other, as you hauled a mountain of files to your desk—\n“If only she… were here…”\nA figure always floats into your mind, a blurry figure with light orange braids, smiling as she kicks those files—which to you feel like a small mountain—into her bag. Then you find yourself nestled in the palm of her hand, placed on her desk like a stuffed animal, watching her complete, bit by bit, the work that should have been yours. \n“All done… Want to grab a bite? Or… how about I eat you?”\nIt seems you can still hear her teasing as she leads you to the night market that’s recently started catering to Giantesses. All the other Giantesses avoid you like the plague, but she’s the only one smiling—even as she’s already threaded your clothes onto the bamboo skewer she’s holding. \n\n“She… must be someone pretty important to me, right?”\nAs if suddenly coming to your senses, you opened the notebook you’d been keeping tucked away in your drawer—an orange cover adorned with playful stickers. You flipped through the pages, only to find… nothing inside? What’s going on? You began to feel anxious, flipping through the pages, but found only this one sentence on the title page:\n“Try to find ‘yourself’ and chase after your own ‘tomorrow.’”"
+  gts_ora.1005.a.custom: "“It looks like there’s been a change in what she gave you. Open it and take a look.”"
+  gts_ora.1007.name: "In Search of \"Her\" Past"
+  gts_ora.1007.desc: "Her past remains a mystery—and how difficult is it to uncover the history of a Celestial Giantess? So you decide to search the cosmos for any information about “Ora,” but she has vanished without a trace, as if she’d evaporated into thin air. \nThirty years have passed—what has become of her? Does she even still exist? You have no idea, but just when you feel at a loss, one day, out of boredom, you flip through that notebook and suddenly come across this sentence—it looks like… the beginning of a diary entry, or perhaps a date?\n“2021… Lone Star…” n\n(Are you ready to learn about “her” past?)"
