+  gts_ora.1008.name: "Lone Star"
+  tradition_gts_ora: "Lone Star"
+  gts_ora.1008.desc: "“2021… Lone Star…”\nYou know this planet—with that enormous straw piercing right through it. Under her governance, the original urban planning meant you didn’t have to worry too much about expenses. It’s just that… you still remember there was one area that wasn’t included in her development plans. \n“This place… let’s just consider it a little bit of private space for us…” nFor a Celestial Giantess to own an area of less than 500 square kilometers clearly doesn’t violate any regulations. It’s just that… she’s obviously been keeping something from you. When you arrived in this area, you discovered—\nIt was just a city—or, to be precise… a metropolitan area from the late stages of the Third Industrial Revolution."
+  gts_ora.1009.name: "Incompetence"
+  gts_ora.1009.desc: "April 2021\nOn the very first day of my 18th year, I was involved in a serious car accident. Fortunately, I survived, but it still affected my college entrance exams. \nI no longer have any regrets. In the split second I was thrown from the car, my mind raced. It seemed as though I saw the city crumbling, traffic coming to a standstill—as if the entire city had become so insignificant at the feet of a single girl. But… so what? In this life of mine, when will I ever lower this head that’s always been held high?\nBut… what if… what if I were that girl myself…\nDecember 5, 2024\nA lot has happened recently, and I’m exhausted. \nBad luck has been piling up, but I finally managed to scrape together enough to buy my own tablet—500 yuan, but surely that’s enough to make my dream come true, right?\nThat image that keeps popping up in my dreams… a girl with a braided ponytail, the entire city at her feet, looking so tiny. It seems that if she were to lift her foot, it would be enough to strike fear into a city, a country, or even the entire planet…\nMaybe the soles of her shoes should be a little thicker… It’d be best if she wore some puffy socks too, so no one could possibly climb up her legs… As for her coat… should it be draped loosely or tied at the waist? Let’s see which one is easier to draw…\nMarch 16, 2025\nI’ve been thinking about this every single moment—about the day I become this person, or rather, the day I can create her with my own hands.\nNow, the time has come. It’s a bit rough around the edges, but time will slowly polish her. \nAs for her name… let’s go with ■■■. Female, age 17… That’s all for today. \nMarch 25, 2028\nHello, everyone! Today is ■■■’s very first live stream~ Let me see how many viewers we have… n15 viewers—not bad for a debut stream. Let’s keep up the good work. \nApril 2028…\nThe author of this diary will likely be unable to continue writing, so I’ll take over. \nJust today, 15 days after virtual streamer ■■■ officially debuted, I saw her in the livestream room with my own eyes. She suddenly stopped her passionate performance, and it wasn’t until thirty minutes later… that we could hear the faint sound of an ambulance in the livestream. \nWhy didn’t she call for help? I don’t know—I don’t know who could even ask that question. Just moments ago, she was diagnosed with acute heart failure and pronounced dead after resuscitation efforts failed—or, to be precise, resuscitation was abandoned. I suppose she simply couldn’t afford the medical bills. \nThe paintings she left behind have become worthless scraps of paper, and the articles she wrote have been swept into the internet’s trash bin. Her existence and her death have become so insignificant to everyone, as if she were a bedbug casually trampled underfoot…\nThen why did she still pursue such an illusory thing?\n……\n“I’m afraid… I won’t live to see the day… when you shine brilliantly among the Stars…” n\nThis is a diary you found in an old residential building, along with an unpublished report. Is this… her? If her past was nothing but death… then that Celestial Giantess you saw was—\nYou dared not think it, but suddenly you heard a voice saying—"
+  gts_ora.1009.a: "I'm here—leave it to me."
+  gts_ora.1010.name: "Illusion"
+  gts_ora.1010.desc: "“Long time no see, everyone!”\n“■■■, which has been on hiatus for a long time, is now back as ‘Giant Girl’~”\nHer pale orange double braids appeared high above the entire planet, all because of a certain insignificant belief. The entire sky was like a holographic screen, and this time, her audience numbered a staggering 9 billion.\n“All right, all right, don’t be afraid, and don’t use any weapons… I won’t hurt any of you…” After a brief self-introduction, the girl vanished among the Stars. And she, too, was searching for an answer—the first question in the world:\n“Who am I?”\n\n“I am ‘Harvest,’ the tomorrow that person was chasing…”\nNow that the person is gone, the girl walks through the cityscape. Everything exists only in that person’s imagination, yet she has never seen his figure again. \nIt’s a bit… ironic.\nGuided by the memories that still lingered, she arrived at an old apartment building. Her body had shrunk somewhat, yet she was still as tall as a ten-story building. Fortunately, it was enough—at least she could crouch down to see what was inside the rooms. \n“I follow the past, but the photographs of the past don’t belong to me…”\n“She rejected me. Then who am I?”\n\n“Sir… how much is this notebook?” n“Five yuan… Oh my God, a monster!!”\nThe girl blocked the entire street—it was just a stationery store, but to her, it looked about the size of a cigarette pack. The shopkeeper’s eyes widened with terror as he watched the girl’s thickened shoe soles block the doorway, cutting off his only hope of escape. \n“Sorry about that… this is the smallest size I have… Here’s your money… my QR code is a bit hard to scan…”\nAfter taking the notebook—which was no bigger than a fingernail—it suddenly changed to a size suitable for the girl, thanks to her power. The girl picked up the pen she’d prepared in advance, sat atop an abandoned building, and stared blankly at the city in the distance. \n“My story… I’ll write it down myself.”\n\nYou picked up the scattered pages you’d found and copied everything into this notebook. You didn’t know the meaning behind doing this; you just had a vague feeling deep down…"
+  gts_ora.1010.a: "Her past life… was starting to become a little clearer."
+  gts_ora.1011.name: "Isolation"
+  gts_ora.1011.desc: "A dreamworld devoid of memory, redemption at the end of the stars, a tower built upon faith…\nThe girl transforms into a hero and charges toward the windmill on the page, and after doing all this, she closes the book, because…\nA group of uninvited guests has arrived at her feet. \nThe girl’s arrival in this world had not caused any destruction. Aside from the occasional panic she sparked among the people when she ventured into the city streets to buy a few things, she spent most of her time sitting in that abandoned district. Amid those crumbling bricks and tiles, it seemed that only this place—far removed from the world of mortals—could serve as fertile ground for the flowers of her imagination. Yet…\nIt seemed this place was not a safe haven for her either.\n\n“No matter where you come from… please leave Earth immediately, or else…” n\nBlatant isolation, rejection of the other—this seemed to be a biological instinct, or perhaps… a reaction born of petty fear. Yet at this moment, it took the form of a 155mm shell, which the girl caught with one hand. Looking down at the metal box at her feet, she sighed. \nThis was the sixth time this had happened, and her patience had finally run out.\nFlinging the small pebble from her fingertip, the girl stood up and gently lifted her shoe—its creator had deliberately made the sole quite thick, likely just to crush these annoying little things underfoot.\n “The monster has shown an aggressive response. Open fire… Hey, hey? Don’t run!”\nHer shoe gently pressed down on the top of the tin box. She applied a little pressure, but it felt just like any ordinary plastic bottle—she sensed no sign of life whatsoever. As for the little creature standing on top of the tin box… …was picked up by the girl, who examined it closely. \nThe twilight cast an orange-red glow over the girl’s braids, outlining her profile in a stunning hue. Yet she was unaware of her own charm; she was simply wondering… why was this little creature’s heart beating so fast? Thump—thump—so this is what it feels like to hold one of these little creatures?\nIt’s so soft, as if it might shatter with the slightest squeeze… Her fingers wanted to squeeze a little more gently, yet she was afraid that if she suddenly let go, the little creature would slip away. In any case, seeing such a tiny creature struggling between her fingers piqued the girl’s curiosity. She wanted to try communicating with it… even if no one would respond. But… she wanted to speak. \n“Um… hello?”\n“Don’t eat me, don’t eat me…”\nThe girl had let her imagination run wild, but it suddenly struck her: “Eat?… What does it mean to eat?” She’d been pondering this question for a while—it seemed she’d never been programmed to eat since the day she was born. That feeling… of being able to put something in your mouth, swallow it, and then digest it in your stomach… Why not try it out on this Tiny person first?\nWith that thought, the girl opened her mouth. Her pink, delicate mouth generously displayed its power of life and death before the Tiny person, her pearly white gums, her quivering soft palate, and the saliva dripping from her upper palate—forming threads within her mouth—resembled a cave, yet carried a citrusy fragrance.\nAs she released her grip, she could already feel a tiny object settle on the tip of her tongue. As it slid deeper along the undulating surface of her tongue, she could sense the Tiny person struggling—like a sailor drowning in the deep sea, forced to watch as the pitch-black ocean floor swallowed him up bit by bit… transforming him from himself into a part of something else…\n\n “She… she’s eating people, isn’t she… she’s tasted our flavor…”\n“Are we… all going to be eaten by her… I don’t want to be eaten…”\n\nIt had no taste, yet like the apple from the Garden of Eden, it was impossible to turn back. The girl licked her lips and began to approach the onlookers. People scattered in all directions, yet their hearts were filled with despair. At this moment, these tiny people were no longer at the top of the food chain—they had become a “snack” for a certain girl.  n\nDid she… ever have this side to her?\nYou dared not think about it, but when you turned and looked up, you saw that enormous straw standing tall in the distance. Standing in this desolate, abandoned urban area, you witnessed the same scene she did, and just like her, you recorded her story."
+  gts_ora.1011.a: "Citrus Blossoms Monologuing in the Wilderness"
+  gts_ora.1012.name: "Panic"
+  gts_ora.1012.desc: "The young girl left the planet where she was born and set out on her journey. But just before she left, out of her own selfish motives, she casually picked up a straw floating in space and stuck it into the ocean on the planet’s surface. \nThe enormous white straw reached up to the sky and plunged straight down to the planet’s core. Everyone witnessed what the girl had done, yet no one dared to speak out. Once upon a time, these people had stood alone against such a colossal figure, but now, after the girl had done as she pleased, everyone realized a problem: nThe long path of godlessness had long lulled these insignificant creatures into complacency, and when this planet finally welcomed a deity of its own—she handed the power of life and death over to Tiny persons to decide for themselves. \nShe no longer took pleasure in the suffering of these Tiny persons; the straw stuck into the planet served merely as a warning—and, incidentally, to take a sip from when she was in a bad mood. Her decision to leave this place was simply to fulfill the dying wish of someone who had entrusted it to her.\n“Amid the glittering Stars.” nShe had seen too much. She had witnessed countless people worshipping a Giantess formed by the convergence of several galaxies, merely to beg for her empire—which would engulf them the moment her lust was aroused. She had seen countless Giantesses, relying on bodies that spanned several continents, trampling the tiny indigenous peoples who had only just emerged from the Stone Age. She saw tiny people regard her as a deity, and more than once, she escaped from the clutches of Giantesses far larger than herself. The young girl, holding a long umbrella and carrying a notebook, recorded everything she experienced among the Stars. \nShe knew of countless deities—beings that transcended this dimension itself. Or perhaps what she saw were merely the forms they projected into this world. She didn’t want it to be this way, yet she was powerless to change it; she felt panic at the thought, yet she continued onward, carrying this emotion with her. \n\n“You don’t really look… like a celestial-level Giantess…”\n“How so?”\n“You’ve been here this long… and haven’t ‘ub’d’ a single Tiny person… Little sister, you can’t be a virgin…” n\nThe girl was, for once, genuinely shocked. Across the entire planet—and even beyond, into the vast expanse far larger than the planet itself—tens of thousands of Giantesses were streaming one after another into the distant, lewd orifice. Just watching from afar, the girl leaned on her long umbrella, barely managing to steady herself and avoid fainting. \nEvery star sea has its own traditions; the girl understood this, and she respected them, yet the panic deep within her heart simply would not go away. Because no matter how much she tried to hide it from herself, she could no longer ignore one issue:\nThe gap between her and everyone else was simply too vast. \nThe story ends here, coming to an abrupt halt. You walk to the shore and gaze at that colossal straw. It seems you can still hear the emotions she felt as she did all this—the pain of being isolated by everyone. \nYou know that during her time in the Empire, she was constantly on the go, busy dealing with envoys from neighboring nations. It’s hard to imagine her as a quiet, reserved person, and you rarely saw her destroy any cities or planets. \nThe more isolated one has been, the more one cherishes the affection one has gained. To the point of being extremely cautious—so unless it’s something truly important…\n“Then why did she choose to leave in the first place?”\nAnd there’s another question I’ve wanted to ask from the very beginning"
+  gts_ora.1012.a: "“Who is she?”"
+  gts_ora.1013.name: "Losing Myself: The Supreme State After Falling into “Nothingness”"
+  gts_ora.1013.desc: "How can one bridge the gap between people—or rather…\nHow can one bridge the gap between insects and deities?\nThe young girl held up her lamp and combed through the timeline one by one. Then, she came to realize a tragic reality—an answer:\nIt was not “no,” yet it was even more terrifying than “no,” and it would require an immense sacrifice. \nShe saw what she would become in the future—pointing her sword at the Milky Way, unafraid of the gods. Yet when she traced back to her past, it was a blank: her future was the future of her past, yet her past was no longer the past of her future.\nShe willingly abandoned everything. \nThis power, known as “Supremacy,” could overturn the entire order of the Milky Way at will. Yet the price was all the past she had ever experienced. She was just one step away from the endpoint she had reached; all she had to do was cast aside the past entirely and retain only the “endpoint”… nShe hesitated, for this raised a single question:\n“Who am I?”\nIf all the planks of a ship were stripped away, leaving only an empty keel, would anyone still recognize it as a ship? The same principle applies. If she were to cast aside every story that belonged to her, would she still exist in this world? She hesitated, and after a moment’s thought, she decided:\nShe wanted to go home—to return to that lonely star. \n\nYou already know the rest of the story: after she returned, she accidentally swallowed an Imperial research vessel. And that’s when you and she first met. Her image gradually began to take shape in your mind: nIt was something you could never have imagined in a lifetime. When she emerged from the stomach of a Celestial Giantess and decided to join you, her pale orange braids wrapped around you, enveloping both you and the entire planet in her embrace—and her name, at this very moment, is already bursting to be spoken in your mind: \nOption: “Ora… Long?” n Effect: Triggers a single event\n\nEvent Name: “Long time no see… or… nice to meet you?”\nYour cry, fueled by obsession, echoes through the deserted old town, and then…\n“What’s wrong?” n A familiar voice rings out. You turn around but see no sign of her. Not until you follow the sound and find her. She’s sitting by the door of an abandoned bus, trying to coax a cat nearby to approach her.\n“Ora?” nDespite the years that had passed since your last meeting, Ora hadn’t changed much—except… the moment you made eye contact, you sensed something was off…\nWhy… does she feel so unfamiliar?\n“Have we… met before?”\nThe girl’s question made you instantly realize something was wrong: Is she Ora? Clearly, she is. But she wasn’t the Ora you’d known before—rather… a series of eerie signs forced you to reach this conclusion:\nShe was the “past” Ora, a manifestation born from your obsession. Just as she had been when she first came into being."
