+  gts_ora.1014.desc: "Your cries, fueled by your obsession, echo through the deserted old town, and then…\n“What’s wrong?” A familiar voice rang out. You turned around but didn’t see her. Not until you followed the sound and found her. She was sitting by the door of an abandoned bus, trying to coax a cat nearby to come closer. \n“Ora?” nDespite the years that had passed since your last meeting, Ora hadn’t changed much—except… the moment you made eye contact, you sensed something was off…\nWhy… did she feel so unfamiliar?\n“Have we… met before?”\nThe girl’s question made you instantly realize something was wrong: Was she Ora? Clearly, she was. But she wasn’t the Ora you’d known before—instead… a series of eerie signs forced you to reach this conclusion:\nShe was the “past” Ora, a manifestation born from your obsession. Just as she had been when she first came into being."
