+  gts_ora.10001.desc: "“Ora?”\nAfter enduring countless hardships, you finally caught sight of Ora, but…\nShe’s changed… quite a bit.\nHer height… is so immense it’s hard to gauge, and her clothes have changed accordingly, though her outer coat is now tattered and worn. and all its decorations have been completely lost. She simply drapes the coat behind her, holding a giant sword in one hand and a battle flag in the other. Upon seeing you arrive, she chooses to shield you behind her—even though you can sense she is already completely exhausted. \nNot a single star remained in the sky; they had all been reduced to dust in the battle. Standing opposite Ora was a figure identical to her current self—yet with indigo-blue pupils.\n“You said we would ‘meet again’ one day… It’s just that this timing is a bit inopportune…”\n“It doesn’t matter. You’ve come at just the right time…”\nHer voice had taken on a hint of weariness, yet it carried a mature quality that smoothed out any rough edges. “Have you brought… my ‘past,’ and… my ‘present’?” You handed the notebook to Ora, even as you struggled against the gravity of a Celestial Giantess, and Ora smiled in response, accepting what had always belonged to her. \n“Though there really is one untimely fellow… but all of this should come to an end…”\n The flame of the “Self” was about to die out, but your arrival made it burn brighter than ever before. The girl lunged at the pseudo-god, her body gradually growing immense, expanding to cover a galaxy, then several galaxies, until it stretched to the very edge of the universe, swallowing whole the one who sought to replace her. \n“I used to be an ordinary student at a school… but my journey and my companions have allowed me to stand face-to-face with the gods.”\n“I was alone in the prison of the Lonely Star, but even outside those walls, bonds of connection remained.”\n“I know that fictional dreams will one day fade away… but they are the gentlest refuge beyond reality.”\n“Every living being feels panic—panic at the unknown, panic at the powerful… but there’s always someone who steps forward.” n“And having gone through all of this… what false evidence could possibly call into question my significance as the ‘Self,’ as ‘Ora?’”\nA halo gradually appeared above her head, and one of her pupils turned indigo. A ring galaxy began to form, with the girl’s head serving as its star, orbiting around it… For some reason, your heart felt incredibly conflicted; it seemed… as if you owed this former administrator of yours an apology. \n“Don’t worry… it’s all been resolved… or is it that… the ‘you’ of now—or rather, you—is also ‘panicking’ about something?” \nIt seemed like she was comforting you, or perhaps comforting Mora. In any case, the girl’s fingers wrapped around Mora’s body; it was just a simple hug, yet it gave Mora a sense of security unlike anything she’d ever felt before. \n“I know… we’ve both walked through the same darkness…”\n“But don’t worry—the future is the future of the past… What I’ve been through, you’ll experience one day—or perhaps you’ll embark on a journey far more exciting than this.” nAfter comforting Mora, Ora turned to look at you. Although her frame had grown considerably larger than before, the moment your gaze met hers, you knew: she was still the person you knew so well.\n“How should I put this… After someone has stubbornly quit their job for decades… shouldn’t they…”"
