+  gts_qinwen_anomaly: "The Land of Extreme Cold"
+  gts_qinwen_anomaly_desc: "This is a frozen, uninhabited planet."
+  gts_qinwen.1.desc: "Just as we had imagined, this was a planet of extreme ice, but the frigid ice covering it could not hide the traces of civilization. With a gentle dig of a shovel, the ruins of buildings beneath the snow were revealed, If these are indeed the remains of a civilization, it proves that the snow covering the entire planet fell suddenly after the civilization was established. Looking into the distance, a mountain villa stands out starkly against the snow, appearing particularly striking amid the desolate silence."
+  gts_qinwen.1.a: "Go investigate that building"
+  gts_qinwen.1.a_custom: "Goo-goo, gaga"
+  gts_qinwen.6.name: "Goo-goo, gaga"
+  gts_qinwen.7.name: "Goo-goo, gaga"
+  gts_trait_qinwen4: "Goo-goo, gaga"
+  gts_qinwen.2.name: "Supplementary Notes on a Stroll Through the Frost-Covered Courtyard and Snow-Clad Pavilion"
+  gts_qinwen.2.desc: "However, just as they were less than two hundred meters from the estate’s gates, a shadow suddenly engulfed the entire sky.\nIt was the breathtakingly massive silhouette of a young girl, gliding slowly overhead. The once-azure sky was instantly obscured; the sunlight was completely swallowed up, and the entire ice plain was plunged into gloomy shadow. The advance team’s communicators were instantly flooded with static and interference, and everyone’s heart seemed to stop beating for a moment nThrough the outline of that shadow, via the communicators, we saw a pair of indescribably large, pink eyes peering down through the clouds with a touch of curiosity at the frozen landscape and the researchers on the ground, who looked as tiny as specks of dust\n“Oh my—” \n“Whoa—there are actually little creatures running around on this tiny planet~” The enormous figure slowly descended. The snow on the ice plain was swept up by the air current descending from the sky, forming concentric rings of white mist that spread out in all directions nWhen those pink eyes finally emerged fully from the clouds, everyone instinctively held their breath\nA girl so vast she could clasp the entire sky in one hand. \nHer features were delicate and gentle, her short white hair drifting slowly in the icy air. She looked just like a literary girl who had stepped out of a fairy tale—if one ignored her massive frame, which stretched across the horizon like a mountain range."
+  gts_qinwen.2.a: "The researcher waved at the young girl as a sign of friendship."
+  gts_qinwen.3.desc: "For the young woman standing before you, the very fact that your presence has caused her to put down her book and look at you directly is a sign of respect for both you and the Empire. Fortunately, she remains friendly toward you and does not treat you as some kind of prized ingredient for infusing liquor.\n“So, where do you come from, traveler? And where are you headed? What brings you here today?”"
+  gts_qinwen.3.a.name: "“I am an agent of the Empire, here on a reconnaissance mission. May I ask your name? And how have you managed to survive in such a bitterly cold place?”"
+  gts_qinwen.3.a.desc: "The young woman standing before you is looking directly at you, a smile spreading across her face, as if admiring your courage in facing a creature of a different size. \n“You have great courage, sir! To remain calm in the face of danger—truly the mark of a great man! My name is Qinwen, and I go by the pseudonym ‘Qinwen.’ I am an ordinary collector. Ever since the last Ice Age began, the bitter cold here has been spreading. Unable to bear the thought of leaving this cabinet full of treasures behind, I’ve stayed here. However, as for the strange changes occurring here, I know nothing of the details. The Great Ice Age isn’t a sudden outbreak, but rather a gradual, slow drop in temperature. A client of mine—who is also a dear friend—gave me a jade pendant; it must be what has allowed me to survive in this bitter cold.”"
+  gts_qinwen.3.b.name: "Your story..."
+  gts_qinwen.3.b.desc: "“A story? I don’t have any dramatic tales to tell. Ever since I inherited my father’s antique shop and this house full of collectibles, I’ve been living here in this little mountain villa—until the snow on Hanling began to fall heavier and heavier, blanketing the landscape in white even in summer. After a few years, heavy snow began to fall even beyond Hanling, Naturally, everyone left. Only I was unafraid of the bitter cold; on the contrary, I even mastered the art of growing larger. Once, I grew so very, very large—almost as big as an entire galaxy. The entire galaxy turned white, and all the planets became frozen wastelands. So, I named that galaxy Ningguta.”"
+  gts_qinwen.3.c.name: "Can I come along?"
+  gts_qinwen.3.c.desc: "“I’d be more than happy to do so. Occasionally going out to meet friends through literature and see a bit of the world does no harm and is greatly beneficial to one’s temperament. However, your spaceship won’t withstand the bitter cold of this ten-thousand-li journey. I happened to build a small boat in my spare time; let’s use that for the return trip. With Qinwen, I stand at your service.”"
+  gts_qinwen.fail: "Let's finish the conversation first."
+  gts_qinwen.5.a.name: "How have you been lately?"
+  gts_qinwen.5.a.desc: "“Thank you for your concern, sir. It’s quite nice here—it’s one of the few places where I feel a sense of belonging.”"
+  gts_qinwen.5.b.name: "“I’d like to see the book you wrote.”"
+  gts_qinwen.5.b.desc: "“These are mere trifles, hardly worth keeping. I am truly ashamed to have received your undeserved praise. If it serves as a bit of entertainment, so much the better. This is something I’ve written recently—a story about myself and a friend of mine. If you like it, please take it.” (He pulled out a celestial-grade iron box.)"
+  gts_qinwen.5.c.name: "“Play penguin sounds”"
+  gts_qinwen.5.c.desc: "“Huh? Is that how penguins sound around here? It’s... kind of... makes me want to mimic it...”"
+  gts_qinwen.6.desc: "“Huh? Is that how penguins sound around here? It’s... kind of... makes me want to mimic it...”"
+  gts_qinwen.5.d.name: "How do you get along with the other leaders?"
+  gts_qinwen.5.d.desc: "§R is not under construction§!"
+  gts_qinwen.5.e.name: "That's all."
+  gts_qinwen.6.a: "Coo-coo-ga-ga!"
+  gts_qinwen.7.desc: "“Goo-goo-ga-ga! Oh... I lost my composure there, but that penguin call is actually quite magical. If I could learn it, I might be able to communicate with penguins.”"
+  gts_qinwen.8.name: "\"On a Winter Day: A Warmth All Her Own\""
+  gts_qinwen.8.desc: "Hanling, a small town nestled in the mountains, lives up to its name—every winter, it is gripped by a biting, bone-chilling cold. The phenomenon of “water turning to ice upon contact,” which people in the big cities to the south regard as a miracle, is nothing out of the ordinary here. \nJust as the character “Han” (Cold) suggests, so does the character “Ling” (Ridge). The town is surrounded by mountains, with poor transportation and spotty cell service—by all logic, this should be a sparsely populated, isolated, and impoverished place.\nHowever, reality sometimes defies logic. \nHanling is, in fact, the most accessible place in the entire Ningguta region and the one with the largest population of outsiders. While I wouldn’t go so far as to say it happens every day, every week sees quite a few wealthy businesspeople from the prosperous southern regions arriving here in stretch limousines or private jets. And their sole destination is that small mountain villa at the foot of the hills. \nThe estate is not large; though called an estate, it is actually no bigger than a traditional courtyard house. Yet it boasts beautiful scenery, a pleasant climate, and a landscape that seems almost otherworldly.\nLooking out over the pond, one sees rippling emerald waters and expanses of lotus leaves. Keep in mind that this is the dead of winter, and we’re in the freezing region of Ningguta. For a pond to remain unfrozen and the plants to stay lush and green is almost like a fairy tale. Yet this small mountain villa has managed to pull it off. First-time visitors can’t help but be secretly amazed, but compared to what lies ahead, this minor wonder can only be attributed to “special insulation technology.”\nFollowing the flow of people toward the villa’s main house, the scene is steeped in antique charm. This shop is, in fact, an antique store—albeit one that is world-renowned. \n“Owner, do you have anything special today?”\n“Yes, I do, my guest.”\nLooking into the store where the conversation was taking place, I saw a white-haired young woman sitting at the front desk; she appeared to be barely over eighteen. Yet she handled the countless wealthy merchants at the counter with composure, showing not a trace of youthfulness; her familiarity with antiquities didn’t seem like that of a young girl, but rather that of a veteran who had been in the business for many years. \nShe held an exquisite clock in her hands, its case crafted from gold and stone and adorned with floral and bird motifs, while the dial featured a magnificent rockery; the lapis lazuli waterfall was a masterpiece of craftsmanship. The moment this piece was unveiled, the many astonishing sights outside the door were reduced to mere backdrops. \nJust as the wealthy merchants were about to scramble for it, a single remark from the young girl sent them away, grumbling under their breath.\n“All right, guests, it’s getting late, and my shop is about to close. Please hurry home.”\nUpon hearing the young woman’s words, though some murmured complaints, they all tactfully took their leave. Although it was still only the afternoon, no one dared to cause a scene. Even those who felt resentful could only cast a fearful glance at the young woman before them—an expression that seemed less like reverence and more like sheer fear."
