+  gts_qinwen.9.desc: "“Knock, knock, knock.”\n“Wenwen, I’m here.” nAfter a soft knock on the door, a gentle voice called out. The owner of that voice was the very reason why the young girl had closed up shop early that afternoon.\nThe moment the door opened, before Qinwen could even say a word, she was swept into an embrace.\n“Oh my gosh, I’ve missed you so much!” nKaining hung onto her, rubbing against the crook of her neck like a little kitten. The setting sun streamed in at an angle from behind, casting a warm golden glow over her long, snow-white hair and brightening the entire entryway. \nQinwen stiffened slightly—she was always like this; no matter how many times she was hugged, her first reaction was always to feel flustered. But she didn’t pull away; she just patted Kaining’s back gently and whispered, “I’m just glad you’re back.” Then, standing on tiptoe, she shyly planted a kiss on Kaining’s cheek. \n“Is that it?” Kaining let go of her and puffed out her cheeks in feigned displeasure. “I’ve been running around all day, and that’s all you give me—just one kiss?”\nQinwen looked up at her. Today, Kaining was wearing an off-white cotton jacket, which made her already striking features appear even softer; her eyes and brows were filled with a radiant smile—she was naturally that kind of person, the center of attention wherever she went, capable of lighting up an entire street just by standing there. \nAnd what about herself?\nQinwen instinctively shifted a step back. She knew exactly what kind of person she was—white hair wasn’t uncommon in Hanling, but her own white hair was always overlooked, along with her very presence. From childhood onward, she’d grown accustomed to sitting in the corner of the classroom without being called on, to being the last one remembered when dividing into groups, and to standing right in the middle of a crowd yet feeling as if she were invisible. \nBut Kaining was different. \nKaining was the kind of person who drew everyone’s attention the moment she walked in. Her radiance wasn’t刻意 showy; it flowed naturally, making people want to draw closer. When she first transferred to Hanling, the whole class was abuzz, with both boys and girls vying to be her friend. Qinwen just watched from afar, thinking to herself: Someone like that would never have anything to do with me. \nBut Kaining walked right up to her. \n“Hey,” Kaining said, waving her hand in front of Qinwen’s face. “Daydreaming again. What are you thinking about?”"
+  gts_qinwen.10.desc: "Qinwen snapped back to reality, her face flushing slightly: “N-nothing.”\n“You’re lying.” Kaining leaned in to look at her and suddenly smiled. “Every time you zone out, you’re thinking, ‘How could anyone possibly care about someone like me?’ Isn’t that right?” nQinwen, her innermost thoughts laid bare, lowered her eyes and remained silent.\nKaining chuckled softly, reached out to cup her face, and made her look at her: “How could no one pay attention to you? I do, after all.”\nQinwen opened her mouth but couldn’t say a word. \nKaining’s thumb gently traced her cheek, kneading it as if working dough, until Qinwen’s face turned as red as a tomato. \nQinwen’s eyes stung a little. She wanted to say “thank you,” but the words were stuck in her throat, and she just couldn’t get them out.\n“All right, all right,” Kaining pinched the tip of her nose. “You do have someone who cares about you, don’t you? Aren’t I a person? I’ll be your desk partner in this life, and I’ll be your desk partner in the next—is that enough?”\nQinwen was amused by her words. She blinked hard to hold back the tears of emotion: “No one would ever say they aren’t a person.” nKaining declared with absolute conviction: “For you, if I’m not human, then I’m not human.”\nQinwen looked at her and suddenly felt that void deep within her heart—one that had always been impossible to fill—being warmed, little by little, by something. \nIn truth, Kaining didn’t know—in her eyes, Qinwen was the only person who wouldn’t be scorched by her radiance. That year, when she’d made her way from a southern city to Hanling, she’d seen far too many people approaching her with fake smiles. Only Qinwen sat quietly in the corner, neither deliberately drawing near nor keeping her distance. When she handed her half an eraser, Qinwen took it, whispered “Thank you,” and then earnestly began correcting the mistakes on her exam paper. \nIn that moment, she knew that this girl, whose presence was barely noticeable, was the only one who could make her let down all her defenses.\n“Well…” Qinwen said softly, her face flushing, “Then I’ll kiss you one more time.” nShe leaned in, aiming for Kaining’s cheek, and, like a chick pecking at grain, gave her a gentle peck, then another. \nKaining’s face grew red and warm from the kisses, yet she was smiling more happily than anyone else. She reached out to pull Qinwen into her arms, resting her chin on the top of her head, her voice as soft as melting sugar: “Now that’s more like it.”\n“Little Kaining, let’s go back to the room.”\n“Okay!” nIn Qinwen’s room, the two played together for quite a while longer before finally drifting off into a deep state of slumber—still clinging to each other as they slept. \nIn this world, the story of these two has come to a close. However, in an unknown place, an epic featuring them as the protagonists has only just begun—a grand, sweeping saga set against the backdrop of an entire world."
+  gts_qinwen.11.desc: "“Huff, huff… Ah~ Ha”\nAccompanied by a young girl’s yawn, Kaining slowly opened her eyes. Her lake-green eyes flickered as she searched for Qinwen, but she couldn’t find her. A faint, tickling sensation at her feet became too much for Kaining to bear, so she looked down... There lay an entire miniature town: ancient thatched huts, pavilions and towers in the distance, and a few farmers no bigger than insects, wielding farming tools and swinging them with all their might at Kaining’s little feet clad in white socks. Judging by the style, it looked like Qinwen’s handiwork, but Qinwen generally didn’t possess that kind of ability, so Kaining also—\n “Phew, this must be a dream...”\n“If it’s a dream... then... I guess I can just stomp on them for fun...” nAccompanied by that gentle voice, the delicate white-socked feet—standing over 50 meters tall—shifted slightly, and those tiny farmers predictably became blood-red blossoms blooming beneath Kaining’s feet.\n“Hmm… just like that… and they’re gone.”\n“I killed someone… . Wait, this is a dream... Phew.”\n“If this is a dream, then those buildings...”\nAs if to confirm her thoughts, Kaining, who had been lying on her side, sprang to her feet. And as soon as she stood— but the moment she stood, her 300-meter-tall body forced all the Tiny persons to their knees. After all, a height of 300 meters was an unimaginable scale in ancient times—with no airplanes and no skyscrapers, Kaining’s height at that moment was no different from that of a deity.\n “Phew, they’re all so tiny. I can’t even make them out unless I look closely... I’ll try taking a couple of steps first,” Kaining said as she cautiously shifted her foot. \nTo her, the movement was nothing more than gently extending her foot forward—she hadn’t even fully lifted her ankle. But to the world below her, it was as if the entire sky had suddenly lowered; the tip of her foot, encased in a white sock, slowly descended from a height resembling the clouds.\n“Boom—” nA muffled, thunderous roar exploded between the streets. Kaining froze for a moment. She looked down to see that the thatched cottages, which had been neatly arranged just moments ago, had completely collapsed into a pile of splintered wood and mud, while a shallow pit had formed beneath the tip of her white-socked foot nAnd the tiny persons who had been wielding their farming tools just moments ago were now completely out of sight. \nAll that remained were a few scattered red dots, slowly spreading between the sole of her sock and the ground. \n“Ugh…”\nShe instinctively lifted her foot slightly.\nA tiny speck was stuck to the sole of her sock—it looked like a crushed berry.\nShe stared at it for a moment, then her face suddenly flushed a little.\n“I really… stepped on it.” nShe muttered under her breath, her voice so soft as if she were afraid someone might hear her—but with the sound amplified 200 times... everyone could hear her just fine."
+  gts_qinwen.12.desc: "But soon, she shook her head again.\n“It’s just a dream… just a dream…”\n“It should be okay in a dream…”\nAfter saying this, she looked down at the world beneath her feet.\nThe spot she’d just crushed with her foot was only a small part of the entire street. Further in the distance were many small houses, fields, rivers, and tiny people scurrying about like ants. \nThey had clearly already spotted her. \nMany were fleeing into the distance, while others knelt on the ground, bowing their heads repeatedly. \n“Are they… worshipping me?”\nShe crouched down slightly, gazing at the city below. \nThat single movement alone sent a heavy tremor rippling through the entire earth. \n“Boom—” n Fine cracks appeared in the ground, and several houses that were already on the verge of collapse came crashing down. Kaining froze again. \n“Ah… I’m sorry, I’m sorry…”\nShe hurriedly whispered an apology, but after speaking, she paused for a moment. \n“Wait a minute…” \n“Why am I apologizing to someone in a dream…?”\nShe tilted her head and thought about it—it made sense.\nIf this was a dream, wouldn’t it be just like a video game~?\nWith that thought, she suddenly felt a bit curious. \n“Then… should I try it again~?”\nShe gently lifted her foot. This time, she could see it clearly.\nHer small foot, wrapped in white socks, rose to a height as high as the sky, and her shadow slowly engulfed the entire village. The tiny people seemed to realize something; they began to scatter frantically in all directions. \nWatching this scene, Kaining suddenly felt a little happy. \n“Um… I hope this isn’t going too far…”\nShe hesitated for a moment. \nThen—\nHer foot came down. \n“BOOM!!”\nThis kick was much harder than the last one. \nA large section of houses was flattened outright, their roofs and walls snapping like paper. Dust rose like fog, slowly spreading out along her calves.\nKaining couldn’t help but gasp.\n“Wow…”\nShe looked down at her feet. \nThe street from moments ago had completely vanished.\nAll that remained was a giant footprint. She slowly lifted her foot; the bottom of her white sock was stained with a faint dark mark.\nKaining stared at the mark for quite a while.\nThen, she suddenly smiled softly.\n “It really feels like stepping on sand…”\nA hint of delight crept into her voice; the initial tension and unease seemed to be slowly fading.\nFrom her height of 300 meters, the distant hills looked no bigger than small mounds of dirt,\nrivers appeared as thin lines, and those tiny people… were so small they were almost invisible. \nThe girl gently lifted one foot and wiggled it in the air. \n“So tiny… No wonder I didn’t notice them earlier.” \nShe murmured softly, taking a gentle step forward. \n“Boom—” The earth shook violently once more.\nWith that single step, she had straddled half the village.\nHer heel landed in a field, completely flattening the entire ridge of the furrow, while her toes touched down on another street, where rows of houses vanished as if erased by a rubber eraser.\n“Eh…” n“I just took one step, that’s all~”\nShe suddenly couldn’t help but laugh.\n“So this is what happens~”\nShe took another step.\n“Boom—”\nThis time, she deliberately slowed down a bit. \nHer delicate feet in white socks slowly descended.\nShe could even see the shadow of her foot gradually covering the ground, as tiny persons scattered in all directions like black dots.\n“Hmm…”\nKaining squinted and watched for a moment. \nThen she pressed down gently with her foot.\n“Snap.”\nShe applied a slight pressure with the sole of her foot.\nThe ground caved in like soft mud.\n“…That’s a little strange,”\nshe murmured, but she didn’t stop; instead, she slowly spun around again. \nThe hem of her skirt fluttered gently in the air, and several of the taller towers were blown right over.\nKaining looked down,\na faint, uncontrollable smile gradually spreading across her face.\n“So… I’m this big, huh~ I wish Qinwen were here.”\n“She’d definitely say I’m just messing around again. ”\nAt that thought, she suddenly felt a bit embarrassed, so she lowered her jade-like foot toward the tiny persons staring at her.\n“Boom!!”\nShe wiggled her foot slightly.\n“It’s just a dream, anyway.”\nThis time, she didn’t hold back.\nHer 300-meter-tall body moved slowly through the ancient city."
+  gts_qinwen.13.desc: "Every step was like a god setting foot on the ground. \nHouses, city walls, bridges, fields… \nThey crumbled endlessly beneath her feet. \nAnd that little bit of shyness and hesitation Kaining had felt at the beginning slowly dissipated like mist. \nShe looked down at the world beneath her feet. \nShe chuckled softly:\n“Such a tiny world…”\nShe lifted her foot.\nThat jade-like foot, carrying a faint, sweet, girlish scent, once again covered an entire town.\n“It’s really convenient to walk on like this.” n“Huh?!”\nJust as Kaining was about to take another step forward, her “petite” body suddenly began to glow.\nThe glow didn’t last long.\nKaining blinked and realized she was still standing in the same spot. No, wait—she wasn’t standing in the same spot; she was standing on this land that had been completely transformed. She instinctively looked down, and then...\nThe tiny people that had once looked like ants were now even smaller. So small that she had to squint to barely make out the moving black dots. And the surrounding buildings… the thatched huts, towers, and city walls that she had once been able to recognize at a glance now looked like blurry patches of color, scattered haphazardly across the ground. \nHer original height of three hundred meters had been enough to overlook the entire city, but now, those pavilions and towers had become nothing more than actual anthills in her eyes. \nKaining tried to look down to find the street she’d just walked on, only to discover she couldn’t make it out at all—that street, that footprint, and everything around it had all shrunk into a tiny, blurry speck. \n“Huh?”\nKaining paused for a moment, then suddenly smiled.\n“It’s getting bigger again~ It’s just a dream anyway~”\nHer voice echoed down from the sky, like muffled thunder rolling across the earth. The tiny people who had narrowly escaped the first wave of trampling looked up at the sky and saw an even more terrifying sight—\nOn the horizon, a colossal pillar soaring into the clouds suddenly appeared; they had to crane their necks to the limit just to barely make out its massive outline. Her face was hidden in the clouds; only those lake-green eyes gazed down upon the tiny world. \nKaining raised her hand to examine it. With her palm spread open, she could block out half the sky. She gently flicked her wrist, and a gust of wind swept through the city, tearing the roofs off countless thatched huts, which spun through the air like scraps of paper. \n“Hmm, this wind…”\nShe shrugged her shoulders slightly, looking a bit embarrassed, but soon couldn’t help but laugh. \n“Sorry, sorry, I didn’t mean to~ But…”\nShe tilted her head to look down at the ground; to her eyes, those tiny people were now little bigger than specks of dust. She tried squinting to focus and could barely make out some tiny black dots moving.\n“They’re so small, I can’t even see them clearly~” nShe muttered, suddenly feeling playful.\n“Well… shall I try again?”\nShe lifted her foot, and this time, without hesitation, stomped down.\n“BOOM————!!!”\nA thunderous roar, deeper and more muffled than any before.\n The ground shook violently, and cracks spread outward from the center of her foot; an entire half of the city vanished completely beneath that single step. When she lifted her foot, a massive footprint several meters deep remained on the ground. The soil at the bottom had been compressed until it was as hard and shiny as porcelain, with no trace of any buildings left to be seen. \n “Wow…”\nKaining blinked, staring at the footprint for quite a while before she couldn’t help but laugh out loud.\n“It’s really completely gone, isn’t it?”\nShe set off, beginning to walk through the city. Every step she took was a catastrophe. Houses crumbled beneath her feet, and she snapped a river in two with a single step, causing the water to flood into the puddle formed by the footprint. She walked very slowly, as if taking a leisurely stroll, but every step brought the city one step closer to destruction.\n“Hmm… Is that a tower over there?” nShe noticed a tall tower in the distance, seemingly the tallest structure in the city. Curious, she walked toward it, only to discover upon reaching it that the tower wasn’t even as tall as her ankle.\n“It’s so short,” she said.\nShe extended her index finger and gave it a gentle push. \nThe tower snapped in half at the waist; the upper section plummeted to the ground, crashing into a nearby house and sending a cloud of dust billowing into the air. Watching this, Kaining suddenly found it a bit amusing. \nThe girl slowly crouched down—a movement that sent another tremor through the ground—then extended a single finger and began to flick at the remaining structures. \nWith a light swipe of her finger, an entire street vanished, turning into an earth-yellow streak.  n With a light tap of her fingertip, a mountain crumbled, turning into an earth-yellow streak"
+  gts_qinwen.14.desc: "She was having so much fun that she didn’t even notice the tiny people desperately scurrying away between her fingers. Occasionally, a few groups of tiny persons would run to her feet and poke her white socks with weapons—swords, spears, and halberds—smaller than bacteria. She just felt a slight itch on the soles of her feet; when she looked down, she discovered a small cluster of black dots gathered there. \n“Hmm, that’s itchy~”\nShe gently lifted her foot and rubbed the itchy spot with the toes of her other foot. \nBy the time she lifted her foot again, that small cluster of black dots had completely vanished, replaced by a patch of red blossoms. However, with just one more crush of her jade-like foot, the tiny splatter of blood was ground into the earth’s crust.\n“Ah…” n Kaining froze for a moment, then smiled sheepishly. \n“Sorry about that—it was just too itchy!”\nThere was hardly any remorse in her tone; it sounded more like she was acting spoiled. \nAs she stood up, she suddenly realized she had grown larger again. The city’s outline, which she’d barely been able to make out moments ago, had now completely blurred into a grayish-brown carpet. Rivers had become thin lines, hills had turned into small mounds, and as for those tiny people… she couldn’t see them at all. \n“I’ve gotten bigger again,”\nshe murmured, a hint of delight in her voice.\n“Then… isn’t this world a little too small?” nShe looked down at her feet; the land that had once been a bustling city now appeared to her as nothing more than a patch of muddy ground she could trample at will. \nAfter all, Kaining had become a Giantess standing five thousand meters tall. \n“BOOM————————!!!” nA deafening roar shook the heavens and the earth; the entire world trembled.\nWhen Kaining lifted her foot again, all that remained beneath her was a massive, bottomless footprint. The city, the Tiny people, and everything that had once existed—all had vanished completely. \nShe looked down at the footprint and suddenly smiled softly.\n“Hmm, looks like I stepped a little too hard.”\nShe tilted her head, her lake-green eyes sparkling.\n \n“But it’s just a dream, after all~ It should be fine, right~?\nSince it’s a dream, that means everything in this world is in Kaining’s hands.\nShe now stood at a terrifying height of one kilometer; mountains, cities, and rivers all seemed minuscule beneath her feet. Realizing this, the last traces of hesitation in Kaining’s heart slowly faded away~\nIn their place came pure playfulness.\n“Ha~ Then let’s make it even bigger~ Let this world give me a proper welcome~” nShe laughed softly—what should have been a young girl’s silvery, bell-like murmur became, in the Tiny Person’s ears, her final sound\nNo sooner had the words left her lips than the familiar light, as if understanding her thoughts, rose once more from beneath her feet, enveloping her entire body\nHowever, this time, it was completely different from before n“Hmm…? Ah~♡”\nWithin the light, the girl couldn’t help but let out a soft, delicate moan.\nThe originally pure white light gradually took on a soft pink hue, as deep and profound as a pair of gentle eyes. That color couldn’t help but remind one of Qinwen’s eyes. \nBut at that moment, Kaining had no time to think about any of that.\nShe suddenly realized that her body was undergoing yet another transformation.\n“Hmm…? There…? It’s getting bigger too…”\nA strange sensation slowly spread out from her chest. \nIt was as if some soft, warm force were gently cradling that area.\nKaining looked down.\n“Hmm…?”\nShe realized that her body wasn’t merely “getting bigger.”\nAs her stature continued to grow, the proportions of her figure were also undergoing subtle changes. \nThe rise and fall of her chest was much more pronounced than before. The change didn’t seem to be simply a result of her increasing height; rather, it felt as though some indescribable desire was gradually gathering there. \nHer originally loose, long dress was slowly being stretched taut, the soft fabric outlining her curves more distinctly.\nNow, her bust was nearly as large as a head, making the girl standing ten thousand meters tall appear even more striking—and even more sensual.\n n Kaining’s breath rose and fell gently. \nWith each rise and fall, a faint, sweet scent seemed to fill the air, drifting out softly. \nThe entire world appeared to be enveloped by this gentle fragrance. \n“H-how come even here…” \nHer cheeks flushed instantly. \nAlthough no one around her could possibly see her fully, she still instinctively covered her chest with her hand.\nBut this action—\nonly made her feel the changes in her body even more clearly.\nHer delicate hands, too, had grown to an unimaginable size. \nWhen that delicate hand rested on her chest, the stark contrast in proportions left even her momentarily stunned."
+  gts_qinwen.15.desc: "“Mmm~♡”\nA faint tingling sensation spread from her fingertips.\nKaining never would have imagined that the changes in her body could bring about such a sensation. \nWhat Kaining didn’t realize was that as her breasts grew larger, they also became more sensitive—a sensation those “flat-chested girls” could never understand. Unlike curvier girls, whose breasts had grown from the size of oranges to watermelons, most people would feel an extreme sense of pressure, but Kaining did not. At that moment, she simply wanted to bless the entire world with her massive, jade-like body and the fullness of her breasts.\nBut contrary to the heaviness she’d imagined, she didn’t feel any sense of oppression. That sensation was, on the contrary, as light as a cloud, making her whole being feel somewhat ethereal.\nIt was as if something warm inside her body was slowly overflowing. \nWith that subtle touch, her previously firm curves trembled ever so slightly.\nIn the next instant,\na warm, milky-white liquid flowed out. \nHowever, Kaining’s body had now grown to a colossal ten thousand meters in size. That seemingly soft form possessed unimaginable mass on this scale; her massive breasts alone weighed several trillion metric tons. nThus, the milky-white stream—which should have been gentle—transformed into a flood that swept across the heavens and earth the moment it fell toward the ground\nA rich, milky fragrance instantly filled the air\nThe milky-white torrent surged down the valley\nRivers were filled to the brim, lakes were submerged, and even the distant ocean gradually turned milky white. Mountain ranges collapsed under the impact, and the earth was carved into new gorges. \nFor this planet, the power unleashed by this “release” was even more staggering than all of Kaining’s previous tramplings and destruction combined.  nThe immense pressure even caused a slight indentation in the Earth’s crust.\nViewed from space—\nhalf of the planet had already turned