+  gts_qinwen.102.desc: "Judging from the reports transmitted by the probe, the interior of the ice cave is even more spectacular than imagined.\n\nAt the entrance stands a natural arch encased in ice; the ice is as thick as glass and, illuminated by the searchlight, refracts a crisp, bluish-white glow. Descending along a sloping ice passage for several dozen meters, the space suddenly opens up to reveal the frozen ruins of an ancient battlefield.\nAt the center of the ruins stands a structure resembling an ancient tomb."
