+  gts_qinwen.103.desc: "There was a moment of silence on the other end of the communicator. \nShe didn’t respond immediately, but simply gazed silently at the frame-by-frame footage of the ice cave being transmitted back to her screen.\nAs the explorer carefully cleared away the ice at the entrance, revealing a line of ancient text engraved on the lintel, Qinwen’s gaze suddenly froze.\n nIt was a short phrase written in extremely ancient oracle bone script. Translated, it roughly meant\n“This sword shall not be stained with blood; this life shall not claim glory. May the land remain unharmed, and may the people live in peace.” nThe young girl from the Celestial Realm, who had been acting coy just moments before, softly recited the phrase, her usual languid tone replaced by a rare sense of solemnity\nThe exploration team continued deeper, opening the frozen tomb door. The interior of the tomb was not lavish; it contained only a well-preserved set of remains. Clad in plain armor and clutching a massive shield, the figure lay peacefully upon a stone platform. The four walls of the tomb were covered with dense, intricate inscriptions chronicling the general’s life nDuring the most turbulent era of strife in the ancient kingdom, he had led troops to defend the frontier. At that time, enemy nations repeatedly invaded, and the people along the border suffered greatly from the ravages of war. Yet, at the height of his military success—having won battle after battle—he took the initiative to send a letter of peace to the enemy nation, offering the benefits of trade, intermarriage, and joint water conservancy projects. The enemy commander was deeply shaken and replied, asking for clarification of his intentions. He wrote only one line in his reply: n“What I seek is not military glory. What I seek is for people to be undisturbed while plowing in spring, for no one to burn their grain during the autumn harvest, and for children not to have to pick up arrowheads from the ruins. This is my war.”\nIn the end, both sides laid down their arms and agreed to a ceasefire, bringing peace to the borderlands for more than fifty years. Yet he, on an ordinary winter night, quietly closed his eyes in his border garrison tent\nHe died peacefully, as light as a feather; not even Qinwen, with her vast store of knowledge, knew his story\nQinwen remained silent for a long time nFinally, she gently removed her round-framed glasses, wiped the lenses with the corner of her sleeve, and put them back on. She looked up, and in her pink eyes there remained only a clear and profound sense of respect. When she spoke, her tone was solemn; that archaic, literary inflection flowed slowly from her lips\n“I have always believed that war is a chronic ailment of civilization, one that cannot be avoided. Yet, upon observing this general’s life, I have come to understand, at least in part, that the end of war does not lie in the cessation of killing, but in the people finding peace. What he sought was not victory, but the people’s peace.”\n“This man exchanged his own decision to lay down arms for twenty years of peace and tranquility. We, born among the stars, are quick to ravage the land and destroy cities, yet we may not possess his magnanimity. I am truly humbled and ashamed that I fall short of his example.”\nShe fell silent for a moment, then let out a few soft laughs.\n“Ah… I’m afraid I won’t be able to concentrate on this book today. I must journey to Hanling myself to pay my respects to this man; it would be best to set aside the affairs of the empire for now.”"
+  gts_qinwen.103.a: "\"Okay, go ahead.\""
+  gts_qinwen.104.desc: "She had actually come—and she was of a rare, normal build.\nShe walked slowly down the sloping ice path, her footsteps echoing softly in the vast ice cavern. The exploration team had long since withdrawn, leaving this silence entirely to her. When she stood before the burial chamber, gazing at the inscription on the lintel, she suddenly stopped in her tracks and stood for a long time before the remains clad in plain armor. She said nothing, merely gazing quietly at the serene face.\n“I once believed that war was nothing more than the result of certain people’s self-interest. I viewed the starry sea as a chessboard and all living beings as pieces—the victor holds the pieces, while the vanquished are annihilated. Yet, gazing upon this man’s remains, I now realize just how reckless my own convictions have been.”\n“He never took pride in slaughter. All he sought was for no one to disturb the spring plowing, and for no one to burn the grain during the autumn harvest—these six words were the cause of his entire life’s struggle. Yet we… so readily commit acts of utter destruction in the name of civilization, without ever considering that the ants crushed beneath our feet sought nothing more than this.” nShe stood up, took a step back, smoothed her robe once more, and bowed solemnly with her hands clasped. \n“I, Qinwen, who takes the sounds of birds and the beauty of mountains and rivers as my emblem, am but a humble lover of wine and books; my lifelong passion has been nothing more than a volume of poetry and prose. Yet today, having witnessed the legacy of this gentleman, I realize how shallow I truly am. From now on, I shall take this as a lesson—to fight with caution and to feel remorse when taking a life.”\nThe young woman straightened up and turned to walk out. When she reached the entrance to the tomb chamber, she paused briefly, turned her head, and added softly,\n“Thank you for your guidance.” nThe sound faded into the ice, swept away by the bone-chilling wind. \nBut within Qinwen’s heart, a tiny spark had ignited into a raging wildfire, completely transforming her way of thinking. \n“This time, I will protect everyone.” \nAt that very moment, we received a communication request from Qinwen."
+  gts_qinwen.104.a: "Get connected right away!"
+  gts_qinwen.105.name: "With a body of steel, we safeguard the peace and security of millions of households"
+  gts_situation_qinwen_fleet: "With a body of steel, we safeguard the peace and security of millions of households"
+  gts_situation_qinwen_fleet_type: "With a body of steel, we safeguard the peace and security of millions of households"
+  gts_qinwen.105.desc: "The moment the communication request was established, a vast starry sky appeared on the screen. Amid the starlight, a silhouette so immense it took one’s breath away slowly unfolded\nQinwen had already regained her majestic, celestial-scale form nWith a single finger, she was gently pinching the two poles of a barren planet; her fingertip sank slightly into the crust. The planet groaned under the strain between her fingers, and spiderweb-like cracks began to spread across its surface nThe young woman tilted her head; a familiar, slightly mischievous smile appeared on her face, which filled nearly half the communication screen. Her pink eyes narrowed slightly, and her tone was light and carefree, as if the solemn reflection from moments ago had never happened\n “Ah ha~ Commander, don’t be so tense~ This planet is barren anyway; it won’t hurt to just play with it a little~”\nAs she spoke, she gently pinched the planet’s poles again, and the crust emitted a crisp cracking sound.\n “I was serious about what I said earlier, you know~ ‘This time, I’ll protect everyone.’”\nShe paused for a moment, then gave her fingertips a gentle twist, causing the planet to spin slowly between her fingers.\n “So—Commander, I’d like to become one of your Fleet Girls.”\n“What do you think? Taking in a ‘Fleet Girl’ who loves drinking, reading, and occasionally crushing a planet or two to pass the time… isn’t too bad a deal, is it~?” nWith a slight squeeze of her fingertips—the barren planet finally shattered completely between her fingers, turning to dust, while her immense figure, shrouding the stars, awaited our response\nShipgirls are an invaluable resource to the Empire; the various fleets we’ve painstakingly built, wouldn’t last a second under the delicate fingers of this celestial-scale maiden. If we could harness Qinwen’s power, it would be like adding wings to a tiger. After all, she only needs to blow a few breaths or stomp a few times to inflict severe damage on the entire Stellar Thread—not to mention, she also possesses the ability to grow to gigantic proportions."
+  gts_qinwen.105.a: "Um... we're a little short on cash right now. Let's wait a bit."
+  gts_qinwen.106.name: "Armor Laying"
+  gts_qinwen.106.desc: "The Empire’s top engineering team had been waiting in orbit for a full half hour. When Qinwen’s massive figure slowly descended from the starry sky, all the staff members instinctively held their breath nAlthough they had seen images of her countless times, the overwhelming sense of awe they felt upon witnessing a celestial-level young woman’s form straddling their homeworld was still something no words could convey. \nShe hovered in the center of the hangar, her arms slightly outstretched, cooperating with the staff as they took measurements. Her pale, jade-like legs hung naturally downward, and her enormous pink sneakers were almost touching the homeworld—and if they were to actually make contact, it would spell utter disaster for the entire Empire. nThe Chief Engineer stood on the command tower, looking up at the figure that nearly obscured half the dome of the spaceport. \nHeavy alloy armor plates were slowly hoisted into the air by a giant crane. Each of these armor plates was as large as half a city and thick enough to withstand the bombardment of a flagship’s main guns. Yet when they were hoisted in front of Qinwen, they seemed insignificant in comparison to her massive frame. nQinwen tilted her head slightly to glance at the armor plate about to be secured to her shoulder blade. She blinked and whispered with a hint of curiosity\n“Hmm… won’t this be a bit heavy to wear?” n“Rest assured, Miss Qinwen,” the chief engineer’s voice came through the communicator, tinged with a touch of nervous deference. “The armor has been lightweighted and won’t hinder your movements.”\n“That’s good to hear~”"
+  gts_qinwen.106.a: "Keep up the good work! There's always plenty of funding."
+  gts_qinwen.106.a_custom: "The research vessel \"Qinwen\" is set to undergo an upgrade"
+  gts_qinwen.107.a_custom: "The research vessel \"Qinwen\" is set to undergo an upgrade"
+  gts_qinwen.108.a_custom: "The research vessel \"Qinwen\" is set to undergo an upgrade"
+  gts_qinwen.107.name: "Ship Gun Installation"
+  gts_qinwen.107.desc: "As the work progressed, more and more armor plates were installed on her torso and limbs. The white coat was gradually covered by silver-gray armor; her arms, chest, sides, knees, and even ankles were all covered with layer upon layer of precision-crafted, sturdy alloy armor. Although the thickness and weight of the armor were enough to crush an entire army, on her magnificent, celestial-scale frame, it looked no more than a beautiful new outer garment. \nNext came the installation of the artillery. \nTwo colossal railguns rose slowly into the air, guided by giant mechanical arms. Each barrel of those two main cannons was large enough to accommodate a destroyer passing through it, and the diameter of the muzzles even exceeded that of the Empire’s grandest parliamentary dome—yet, in the eyes of the colossal, celestial-class girl, they were nothing more than two ring-shaped objects\n “Hmm…” Qinwen looked at those two “rings,” narrowing her pink eyes slightly, her tone carrying a hint of undisguised disdain. “Aren’t these… a bit flashy but impractical?” nOur chief engineer was taken aback: “Miss Qinwen, this is our Empire’s latest orbital rapid-fire cannon. Its firepower is sufficient to destroy an entire fleet with a single shot—” n“I know, I know.” Qinwen waved her hand; the air pressure from the gesture caused all the lights in the entire drydock to sway violently. She lowered her head, bringing her enormous pink eyes close to the command tower, and whispered with a hint of lazy amusement, “ “But—Your Excellency, the Commander, how many seconds do you think it would take me to crush a planet~?” nQinwen raised a hand, her slender, long fingers slowly flexing against the starlit sky. In an instant, an innocent little asteroid became nothing more than dust between the girl’s fingers. “Instead of mounting all those clunky cannons, why not let me just flick it gently with this finger—the effect won’t be any worse than your cannons, you know~.” nA bead of cold sweat formed on the Chief Engineer’s forehead, but he persisted: “Miss Qinwen, this is the standard outfitting procedure for Imperial Ship Girls. Please cooperate—” n“All right, all right, I’ll install them then~” Qinwen sighed, her tone tinged with a touch of indulgent resignation. “Just think of it as putting on a ring~”"
+  gts_qinwen.108.name: "Completed"
+  gts_qinwen.108.desc: "After our tireless efforts, the transformation of the Celestial-Class Literary Girl has finally been successful, and she now stands before her homeworld, receiving a review from the people. nShe gently moved those two “rings”—the two massive orbital cannons capable of destroying an entire fleet—which rotated slightly between her fingers, their barrels pointing directly at the homeworld, causing a wave of panic.\nShe heard the faint yet passionate cries rising from the surface, piercing through the atmosphere.\n “Hmm… It feels a little embarrassing to be watched by so many people~ I think I’ve scared the little ones.”\nAs she spoke, she did not avert her gaze; instead, she tilted her head slightly, turning her face directly toward her homeworld. That enormous, exquisite face glowed in the light of the stars and the stardock’s lights, like that of a deity. \nShe slowly raised her slender hand, lightly touched her lips with her fingertips, and blew a kiss—unaware that a few droplets of saliva had splashed onto the planet. \n “Hey~ little ones~”\nHer voice came through the communicator and was broadcast to public channels across the homeworld. Her voice was soft and tinged with a touch of playfulness, like a neighbor’s older sister waving to the children below from her windowsill.\nOn the ground, an even more enthusiastic cheer erupted. The few droplets from the young woman’s breath transformed into the largest lake, ensuring that the arid regions would have no shortage of water for decades.\n nShe even tilted her head down, lowering her enormous face slightly so that the people on the ground could see her features more clearly\n“All right, all right, stop staring at me~” she whispered with a touch of feigned petulance, “ “But… if you’d like, every time I return from a mission, I can stop by Starport to say hello to everyone~”\nQinwen’s cheerful smile touched everyone’s hearts. With such a gentle yet powerful leader among the Ship Girls, the Empire would surely be even stronger."
+  gts_qinwen.111.desc: "In the Ningguta Star System, which is entirely frozen over, there are still a few habitable planets. Through our tireless efforts, several of these planets have been successively transformed and settled by a large population, greatly alleviating the population crisis in other star systems. And Qinwen—that colossal literary maiden—is now sitting right here on the top floor of this planet’s shopping mall, leisurely savoring the pleasant afternoon. \nQinwen, who is usually the size of a celestial body, is now only a few dozen meters tall. \n“Wine is the source of civilization,” She raised her enormous wine glass, which resembled a hill; the amber liquid shimmered with a golden glow in the dazzling sunlight. “Without wine, how could such a wonderful civilization have come to be?” nHer slightly tipsy, rosy eyes narrowed ever so slightly, radiating a mix of rapture and languor, as she cast her gaze down at the street below. Her enormous sneakers, a blend of pink and white, hovered directly above the plaza on the ground floor of the mall. Her legs swayed with each breath, and the thick, pristine soles—to the citizens of civilization below, who seemed as tiny as ants—formed a vast dome that blocked out the sky. nQinwen suddenly felt a surge of playfulness\nA faint smile tugged at the corners of her mouth as she gently swayed her legs; the massive sole swept through the low sky, and the resulting air currents sent dust and fallen leaves swirling wildly across the plaza below. The tiny people screamed in panic and scattered in all directions, only to be completely engulfed by the shadow cast by that wide rubber sole.\n“Oh my, you tiny ones sure can run fast~” She muttered to herself, slightly tipsy, and slowly lowered the ankle encased in a white sock—gently scraping the edge of the shoe against the brick pavement at the edge of the square nYet this utterly trivial, playful gesture was, to the tiny persons below, a sky-shattering, earth-shattering storm. The intense friction generated a powerful gust of wind; several of the slower tiny people were knocked to the ground by the airflow sweeping from the side of her shoe, tumbling and scrambling several meters away\nQinwen, however, seemed completely oblivious, merely flashing a girlish smile—innocent yet slightly mischievous. She raised her giant foot once more, gently tiptoeing on the sole adorned with soft pink patterns, causing the tiny people below to look up in fear and anxiety as they were enveloped by the shadow cast by her shoe\n “Looking down from on high as civilization flourishes, screams, and scatters beneath my feet… seems like an even better accompaniment to my drink than the stories in books~” She took a leisurely, large gulp of ale; the sweet liquid trickled down her fair chin and splashed onto the mall’s rooftop, drowning several Tiny people in the beer."
+  gts_qinwen.111.a: "Hurry up—while she’s still sober—and get everyone out of here."
+  gts_qinwen.112.desc: "The roar of the ships’ engines gradually faded into the thin atmosphere, and the last batch of transport ships, trailing long plumes of exhaust, plunged into the clouds. The planet, once bustling with life, was now plunged into complete silence.\nHer pink eyes were half-closed, their gaze hazy and languid from the alcohol. She looked down at the deserted city below and let out a light, slightly amused chuckle~\n“Oh my~ I can’t wait—they’ve evacuated everyone so quickly~” nThe young girl slowly raised one hand, gently resting her jade-white fingertip on the ground at the edge of the city. Her fingertip sank into the soil and reinforced concrete, emitting a dull crack. She tilted her head slightly and murmured\n“So, are you planning to create an amusement park for me, Your Excellency~?” Her voice took on a lighter tone. “In that case, I shall humbly comply~” nNo sooner had the words left her mouth—accompanied by a low rumble—than she began to grow even larger once more\nYes, even though she was already a colossal presence, she continued to expand without hesitation. Her fingers grew even more colossal, and her body spread out among the mountains. The city, which had originally been crushed under her weight, had now transformed into mountain ranges. Her calves and ankles stretched endlessly into the clouds, and her pink-and-blue sneakers were now so enormous that an entire river had to detour around the soles. nThe girl leaned down, pressing her cheek close to the ground; her dreamy pink eyes were almost touching the spire of one of the skyscrapers.\n“Hmm… The world has suddenly become so small, just like that exquisite miniature model on my desk.” nShe stuck out the tip of her tongue and gently licked away the lingering scent of wheat beer from the corner of her mouth, then pressed that finger—as massive as a mountain range—~gently~ and slowly onto a city block\n “Well… I’m going to have some fun—slowly and thoroughly—at this amusement park~”\nShe slowly raised herself up, her massive form casting a shadow across the planet’s horizon that spanned nearly half the hemisphere. The mountains beneath her had turned into rolling hills, and the soles of her massive, heavy sneakers hovered above what had once been the bustling heart of the city.\nAnd after a few rounds of drinks, the flush on Qinwen’s face grew even deeper."
+  gts_qinwen.112.a: "It's a good thing we acted quickly—it was truly shocking."
+  gts_qinwen.113.desc: "“Ah~ I guess no one’s around anymore~”\nShe let out a lazy burp; the breath, carrying a rich malt aroma, swept across the planet’s surface, blowing away the layer of clouds that had been hovering low in the sky and revealing the city ruins below in even greater detail.\n “Hmm… this position feels pretty good~”\nQinwen narrowed her half-drunken purple eyes, gently propping herself up, allowing her astonishingly supple breasts to slowly swell, growing, transforming her once-barren chest into a proud, almost mocking mass that pressed down upon what had once been the planet’s most prosperous continent.\nThose enormous, full breasts slowly descended upon the urban landscape. Her movements were elegant, stirring the blood, and even carried a girlish, carefree lightness—yet when her soft chest and abdomen touched the ground, hundreds of square kilometers of the steel jungle sank silently, shattered, and turned to dust, then completely buried beneath that layer of fair skin and fabric\nShe glanced down at the flattened “little square” beneath her, her expression betraying a pure, domineering delight~\n“This whole area’s been flattened, hasn’t it~” nShe showed no intention of getting up; instead, she shifted her weight slightly with the arms braced against the ground, allowing her breasts—soft as cotton clouds—to gently rub against the rubble nThe few remaining skyscraper spires were completely crushed into the earth’s crust by that “gentle kneading.” And at the very edge where her areolas met the ground, the immense weight and pressure caused the earth to bulge outward in waves, forming a ring of mountains that stretched all the way to the horizon\n“It seems~ that area over there hasn’t been blessed by Big Sister yet~” nShe applied a slight amount of force with the arms braced against the ground, shifting her massive body dozens of kilometers across the planet’s surface—a movement that was merely a lazy roll over for her, but for the planet, it was a devastating upheaval between continental plates. \nHer soft breasts rolled across the ground, completely flattening the already shattered city ruins into a smooth, slightly curved indentation; the resulting shockwaves forced groundwater from deep within the crust to the surface, flooding everything nShe rolled over again, settling into a half-reclining, half-seated position, and once more suspended her enormous breasts above the coastal plain. Then, with an incredibly innocent, playful lightness, she began to gently pinch her massive nipples...\n“Ooh~” nShe let out a soft, drunken interjection, and a few drops of milk oozed from her two erect nipples\nThis time, simply letting the relaxation brought on by alcohol take over, she allowed her body’s weight to sink down naturally. Yet her supple breasts, strong enough to support her massive frame, submerged all the skyscrapers across the coastal plain in a manner so gentle it bordered on cruelty nThose once-precise skyscrapers and industrial facilities were gently flattened under the pressure of her chest, leaving behind only a shallow white indentation bearing the imprint of her body heat and the texture of her fabric nShe seemed quite satisfied with this result; she even gave her waist a gentle twist, using the ground—which had been flattened to the point of nearly reflecting sunlight—as support to adjust into a more comfortable position— —her enormous sneakers dangled in the air, then swung back down, crushing several isolated peaks in the distance that hadn’t yet collapsed into dust, the debris scattering across the ground beneath her—a landscape already rendered unrecognizable... n“Ah… I really shouldn’t drink too much~. If I’m not careful, I’ll end up doing something… hmm~… slightly~ a bit excessive~.”\n“I’ve crushed everything everyone worked so hard to build… So, to make it up to this little planet… I’ll give it a gentle~, giant hug~.” n\n\nNo sooner had the words left her mouth than her form began to expand once more.\nIt was such an elegant and silent growth—the jade-like body that had once dominated the continent now enveloped the entire planet."
+  gts_qinwen.114.desc: "She slowly cradled the blue planet in the palm of her hand.\nShe looked down at her hand, which was growing larger and larger, and at the planet, which was gradually becoming smaller and smaller in her palm. The corners of her mouth slowly turned upward, revealing a smile that was both gentle and heart-stopping. nShe gently raised the planet before her, and then —as if to fulfill the promise of a hug she’d just made—slowly and with boundless tenderness, she drew the planet close to her soft chest, gently pressing it against her, embracing the entire planet that had once sustained countless lives into her arms... n“Snap.”\nAn extremely faint, crisp sound came from between the layers of fabric on her chest and the flattened planet. nQinwen paused slightly and looked down—the blue planet, under the gentle pressure of her soft breasts, which had swelled to rival a star in size, was already showing clear cracks. The cracks spread from the surface to the mantle, from the oceans to the clouds; the entire planet’s structure was quietly collapsing within that casual embrace against her chest\nShe smiled softly, with a touch of mockery. She slowly released her embrace, watching the planet—already shattered into pieces—slip from her chest, its fragments scattering like shooting stars between her ever-widening knees and the hem of her skirt. With a gentle pinch of her fingers—the once-intact planet completely dissolved into a handful of fine dust at her fingertips, rustling as it fell through her fingers and merged into the endless, dark starry sky beneath her The celestial-class maiden raised her head slightly, her pink eyes twinkling in the sea of stars. Her jade-like form continued to grow silently, drawing the stars of the entire star system one by one into the shadow cast by her figure. “Hmm… Sorry about that~ Next time… I’ll be just a little bit gentler~.”"
+  gts_qinwen.114.a: "“Use the remnants of her wine as the foundation for the planet and reshape it.”"
+  gts_qinwen.114.b: "“Oh, my planet! Just you wait—I’ve got a way to deal with you!”"
+  gts_qinwen.120.name: "First Attempt at Creation"
+  gts_qinwen.120.desc: "It’s been well over a few months since Qinwen last crushed that planet in the Ningguta Galaxy. And the footage we risked our lives to capture—which documented how Qinwen completely destroyed that planet with her breasts—must surely be enough to keep this usually elegant and image-conscious literary girl blushing and shy for quite some time. \nThe moment the call connected, that familiar face appeared on the screen. \n “Ahaha… Commander, is there something you need?” nThe white-haired girl scratched her head, her eyes darting about, a hint of awkward yet polite smile playing at the corners of her mouth\nShe must know why we’re contacting her\nHowever, we all know full well: Qinwen’s tolerance for alcohol is terrifying. That amount of beer alone certainly wouldn’t have left her completely drunk. So, whether that alcohol-induced haze she displayed that day was an act—or whether she truly, from the bottom of her heart, enjoyed the sensation of that planet shattering beneath her fingertips—remains to be verified\nWe projected the high-definition footage onto the communication interface. The footage opened with Qinwen’s two massive breasts—her breasts pressing everything flat before shattering.\nQinwen’s face flushed red in an instant. Her red eyes widened in shock.\n“T-this… this is…” She stammered, her voice growing fainter and fainter. “This… that… I was just drunk at the time…”\nThe tips of her ears were so red they looked as if they might bleed. She sat there, completely at a loss, her head bowed.\n“How… how did you even record this…? This is so embarrassing…” n“Miss Qinwen, we’ve already made a backup of this video. If you ever act out like this while drunk again within our jurisdiction, this footage might be made public throughout the entire star system as part of the Imperial Security Archives.” nShe jerked her head up, and the shyness in her pink eyes was instantly replaced by a hint of panic\n“Huh?! P-publicly?! No, no, no!!! T-that’s so embarrassing! !! I’m a writer, for heaven’s sake—how could I let everyone see me… me… like that…”\nFrantic and embarrassed, the young woman began to stutter as she frantically waved her hands in front of the communication screen.\n“Of course, we’re not unreasonable people. If you’re willing to cooperate with us on a few things... and guarantee that you’ll never again... um—‘actively destroy a planet that’s been modified for human habitation,’ this file can be permanently sealed.”\n“Th—then what do you want me to do? Just so we’re clear, I’m not doing anything too tiring.”\n“Don’t worry, it’s nothing difficult—it seems your breast milk could serve as the foundation for the new planet...” nQinwen froze for a moment, then her entire face flushed bright red again. She grabbed the book next to her and hurled it toward the communicator’s camera, shouting indignantly\n“You bunch of scoundrels!”\n“Oh my~ So, are you willing, Your Excellency?”\n“Fine… All right.”\nOption: Squeeze!\nOut in the vast sea of stars, Qinwen had returned to her celestial-scale size, kneading her magnificent breasts with both hands, while we periodically fired our cannons at her, intensifying her pleasure. After some time had passed, we could tell from the look on her face that a new planet was about to be born in this galaxy.\nShe gently pinched her erect breasts; the squeezing of her slender hands, combined with our artillery attacks, soon caused a few milky-white drops to spill from her chest. Those few drops of milk were insignificant to Qinwen, but to us, they were already the size of a planet. With just a little time, we could make up for the loss of that planet, and a hint of the pleasure of “creating a world” also appeared on her completely flushed cheeks..."
+  gts_qinwen.121.desc: "After our tireless efforts, we finally transformed a few drops of Bird Sound’s milk into a habitable planet. nThe planet’s natural ocean of milk will provide drinking water for its citizens for a long time to come. The loss of the previous planet has been made up for, and the celestial-level maiden is gazing at the planet with a blush on her cheeks, seemingly deriving a hint of pleasure from it... In any case, this is of great benefit to the Empire."
+  gts_qinwen.121.a: "That's great!"
