diff --git a/localisation/english/leaders/gts_i_seele_li_l_english.yml b/localisation/english/leaders/gts_i_seele_li_l_english.yml
index b230dae..ae3aafa 100644
--- a/localisation/english/leaders/gts_i_seele_li_l_english.yml
+++ b/localisation/english/leaders/gts_i_seele_li_l_english.yml
@@ -1 +1,64 @@
-l_english:
\ No newline at end of file
+l_english:
+  gts_seele_li.3.name: "Close"
+  gts_seele_li.1.name: "Start"
+  gts_seele_li.1.desc: "The outpost at [event_target:gts_azure_waters_system.GetName] detected a strange energy fluctuation that, upon verification, bears a striking resemblance to the energy emitted when an Astral Rift forms. We have also observed the formation of a rift here, but it is clearly extremely unstable; strange entities keep surging out of it, only to vanish into the void immediately. These intermittent energy surges leave no doubt that something massive is approaching. Whether it’s a new Star Beast or a Giantess, we must prioritize our own safety first…"
+  gts_seele_li.1.a: "Help \"her\" get rid of"
+  gts_seele_li.1.a_custom: "\"Exploring the Fissure\" is part of the subsequent content; you must recruit either §R Seele§! or §B Seele§! before you can proceed."
+  gts_seele_li.1.b: "Seal this off"
+  gts_seele_li.1.b_custom: "You will obtain a large amount of physics, astral threads, and dark matter. §R But this will bring the Indigo Sea Group event chain to an end!§!"
+  gts_seele_li.2.name: "Tear"
+  gts_seele_li.2.desc: "After several attempts, we succeeded in significantly widening the “exit” of the fissure. More and more matter is emerging from it, allowing more objects to stabilize before they completely dissipate. At the same time, the research vessels we’ve sent in are able to navigate past these obstructions and venture further into this “brand-new?” space. As for the results… we’ll find out soon enough."
+  gts_seele_li.2.a: "Stay alert"
+  gts_seele_li.2.b: "Start by collecting"
+  gts_seele_li.3.desc: "The material that has been oozing out over time has significantly narrowed the entrance to the fissure, making it increasingly difficult for us to observe what’s happening inside and to track the energy surges that occurred earlier. If we want to continue our exploration, we must try to reopen the fissure."
+  gts_seele_li.3.a: "Give it a try"
+  gts_seele_li.3.b: "Let it stay closed."
+  gts_seele_li.3.b_custom: "§RThis will bring the series of events involving the Ganhai Group to a close!§!"
+  gts_seele_li.4.desc: "We successfully located the source of the energy fluctuations—an unconscious young girl with her eyes closed, her red hair in disarray, and her body covered in wounds. It seemed as though even her “existence” was highly unstable. Based on our estimates, her size falls roughly within what we classify as “Titan-class.” To ensure her safety, the accompanying research vessel decided to bring her back with us first. While this decision inevitably slowed down our exploration of the fissure, we believe it was well worth it. \nThe red-haired girl has been placed on a desolate planet, accompanied only by a medical team and a science officer. We expect a more detailed medical report to be delivered shortly…"
+  gts_seele_li.4.a: "Study her condition"
+  gts_seele_li.4.b: "Continue Exploring the Fissure"
+  gts_seele_li.4.c: "Gather Resources"
+  gts_seele_li.5.name: "Awakening"
+  gts_seele_li.5.desc: "Although the girl’s 100,000-fold increase in body size posed some diagnostic challenges, what truly hindered medical treatment was her physical condition, which left even the research team at a loss. Her body, which fluctuates between a quantum state—as ethereal as a void-spawn—and occasional vanishing into nothingness, provided new material for research. Setting aside these factors, is she actually quite “healthy”? \nBut what’s even more bizarre is that her size has continued to increase since she left the fissure—growing from just 100,000 times her original size to 300,000 times in a single month. Moreover, as her physical condition stabilizes, the rate of growth is accelerating. After relocating the facility several times, the staff in charge simply moved the equipment directly onto her body. \nJudging by the latest data, she may awaken soon… perhaps this month? Or tomorrow…? Right now! The stationed personnel were jolted awake by violent tremors and quickly boarded a transport ship to leave the surface. Viewed from the air, her body had stopped growing and had stabilized at roughly 500,000 times her original size. She now sits on this land, watching the transport ship warily."
+  gts_seele_li.5.a: "Establish a Connection"
+  gts_seele_li.6.name: "§R“Seele?”§!"
+  gts_seele_li.6.desc: "When she awoke from her coma, she felt as if she had lost something precious, and she was on high alert in this environment that was both unfamiliar and familiar."
+  gts_seele_li.6.a.name: "Who are you? You can't just not introduce yourself, can you?"
+  gts_seele_li.6.a.desc: " After a brief silence, the girl—perhaps realizing something was amiss—finally said her name. “§R ‘Seele’ §!”"
+  gts_seele_li.6.b.name: "Why are you in the crevice?"
+  gts_seele_li.6.b.desc: "After a longer silence, instead of an answer, we were met with a new question: “What did you do to me? How is Seele now?!”"
+  gts_seele_li.6.c.name: "We didn't do anything to you"
+  gts_seele_li.6.c.desc: "So how did I come to exist independently of her… Don’t you guys know anything?"
+  gts_seele_li.6.d.name: "I didn't see anyone else. How are you doing?"
+  gts_seele_li.6.d.desc: "How can a shadow even hope to exist apart from its source… Since you guys don’t have any clues either, could you help me get back to the Quantum Sea? Or take me to the “Rift”?"
+  gts_seele_li.6.e.name: "“§B Seele§!” What on earth is that?"
+  gts_seele_li.6.e.desc: "He's such a big dummy who's always trying to act tough but still needs me to protect him! Is that clear now? (Hmph)"
+  gts_seele_li.6.f.name: "I could take you there, but getting back in might be a bit tricky."
+  gts_seele_li.6.f.desc: "“What?” §R “Seele”§! She let slip a look of surprise—a rare occurrence."
+  gts_seele_li.hire_custom_tooltip: "§R \"Seele\" §! is joining us"
+  gts_seele_li.7.name: "Try"
+  gts_seele_li.7.desc: "We returned to the fissure with §R “Seele”§!, but after this period of adaptation and growth, her body was no longer able to enter it, and we had no way to help her proceed. After a moment’s hesitation, §R “Seele”§! made a new request: “Blow up the fissure directly to release the energy inside, causing the surrounding area to briefly enter the Quantum Sea.” She would then search the area so that, as it falls, it would end up near §B Seele§!. In any case, it’s worth a try, isn’t it?"
+  gts_seele_li.7.a: "Let's give it a try, then."
+  gts_seele_li.9.name: "futa content"
+  gts_seele_li.10.name: "Kissing"
+  gts_seele_li.10.desc: "We successfully triggered the explosion at the fissure, and a massive amount of energy surged out uncontrollably. Everything in the galaxy was changing rapidly, as if being swallowed up by this torrent. By the time the surroundings had calmed down, the entire galaxy seemed to have plunged into a sea of quantum energy.\nAnd not far away was §R “Seele”§! The longed-for §B Seele§! looked at the suddenly appearing §R “Seele”§! with some surprise, momentarily at a loss. “Another me? Is that you?”\n“Mm-hmm, don’t be afraid. §B Seele§!, I’m here to take you away from here.”§ R“Seele”§! drew closer, whispering words of comfort to Seele. “Now close your eyes. Leave the rest to me.”\nWatching Seele close her eyes with trust, her body nestled against his chest, §R“Seele”§! gazed at her for a moment before gently kissing her. §B Seele§! resisted somewhat frantically at first, as if she thought her other self was teasing her, but a familiar sense of security and trust still led her to believe in §R “Seele”§!.\nAs §R “Seele”§! deliberate guidance, more and more energy from the surroundings converged on §B Seele§!, and the influence of the quantum sea within the galaxy gradually diminished, allowing her original form to become faintly visible. §R“Seele”§! finally let go of §B Seele§! with a heavy heart, having successfully brought her out of the quantum sea. Looking at the familiar §B Seele§! before her, §R “Seele”§! could not contain her excitement and embraced her tightly once more.\nHowever, due to the earlier explosion that created the fissure, it seemed this scar would never fully heal. And… weren’t they a little bigger than expected?"
+  gts_seele_li.10.a: "At least the outcome was positive."
+  gts_seele_li.11.name: "Cleanup Complete"
+  gts_seele_li.11.desc: "We’ve cleared away a lot of the material that had accumulated in the fissure, so we can try to widen it again. But we must act quickly—the constantly spilling energy will soon seal it shut once more."
+  gts_seele_li.11.a: "Hurry up"
+  gts_seele_li.12.name: "§B Seele §!"
+  gts_seele_li.12.desc: "Having escaped from the Sea of Quantum, I have now joined you alongside §R “Seele”§!"
+  gts_seele_li.12.a.name: "Welcome"
+  gts_seele_li.12.a.desc: "Everyone's so enthusiastic, §B Seele§! I'm actually a little overwhelmed..."
+  gts_seele_li.12.b.name: "§B Seele§! What can I do?"
+  gts_seele_li.12.b.desc: "As long as it's something §B Seele§! can do, §B Seele§! will definitely do her best."
+  gts_seele_li.12.c.name: "About *The Quantum Sea*..."
+  gts_seele_li.12.c.desc: "If possible, §B Seele§! would like to go find §C Bronya§! again..."
+  gts_seele_li.12.d.name: "Do I fit in here?"
+  gts_seele_li.12.d.desc: "Well, §B Seele§'s body will gradually stabilize, and she'll adjust to it soon."
+  gts_seele_li_special_project: "Expansion Crack"
+  gts_seele_li_special_project_DESC: "Clear away the material blocking the area around the fissure so that the research vessel can enter and explore normally."
+  gts_seele_li_anomaly_1: "Open Again"
+  gts_seele_li_anomaly_1_desc: "Clearing away the debris that had accumulated around the crack allowed a small gap to reopen there."
+  gts_seele_li_anomaly_2: "Blast Fissure"
+  gts_seele_li_anomaly_2_desc: "Using the simplest method to widen the fissure, a direct blast is used to trigger the material inside, causing the surrounding area to briefly enter the quantum sea..."
\ No newline at end of file
