+  gts_random_storm.11.desc: "The investigation into the source of the sweat storm has been a success!\nOur scientists discovered an unstable spatial rift at the center of the storm—a rift that connects two distant points in space. Since the two ends of the rift are not the same size, the flow of matter passing through it is magnified or shrunk by hundreds of thousands of times due to spatial distortion. In other words, the galaxies currently being swept up by the sweat storm are, at this very moment, nestled in the armpit of a Giantess. \nOur research vessel has successfully pinpointed the coordinates of the other end of the rift; it appears the rift’s entrance has materialized on the body of a student from a sports academy who has come to one of our colonies. \nWhen our research vessel entered to investigate, this female student was resting. \nPreviously, to cope with the sweat tide, we had restricted natural disaster controls to outdoor sports, so they had moved indoors to continue training nClearly, she had no idea that the massive storm affecting several galaxies actually originated from her own sweat during exercise. \nAs she was about to finish her rest and resume training, the research vessel quickly accelerated away from the armpit world. A few minutes later, another wave of fresh sweat surged out of the spatial rift. \nTo reduce the likelihood of her sweating, the Imperial Administration expanded the natural disaster restrictions to cover all athletic events, limiting the physical training of this girl and her classmates to a basic level so that, with their free time, they could focus on theoretical studies. \nOur scientists predict that this rift is unstable and will close completely within a few months to a few years. However, the sweat storms that have already been poured into the Milky Way through the portal can only be left to time to resolve."
