+  gts_random_storm.44.desc: "The investigation into the origin of the Milk Tide has been a success! \nOur scientists have discovered a twisted spatial rift at the center of the Milky Way Tidal Wave—a rift that connects two distant regions of space. Because the two ends of the rift are of different sizes, the flow of matter passing through it is amplified or Shrinked by hundreds of thousands of times due to the spatial distortion, which explains the origin of this vast Milky Way Tidal Wave. In other words, the galaxies currently being swept up by the Milk Storm are, at this very moment, residing within the mammary glands of a certain woman. \nHowever, upon passing through the spatial rift, the research vessel detected a location signal indicating they were on our Empire’s homeworld—more precisely, within the residence of our homeworld’s Giantess Leader. \nFurther confirmation revealed that... [event_target:gts_random_storm_leader_target.GetName]—the storm affecting several galaxies originated from the milk within her soft breasts. \nThis giant goddess was currently stretching lazily, leaning back on the sofa and perusing documents. What she does not know is that with every breath she takes—or every slight sway of her chest—the tranquil sea of milk within her mammary glands instantly erupts into a raging storm, and a new tide of milk surges forth from a rift in space, flooding the surrounding galaxies. Separated by tens of thousands of kilometers of fat as thick as the Earth’s crust, as well as her bra and blouse, we quietly listened to [event_target:gts_random_storm_leader_target.GetName]’s gentle murmur. If it weren’t for the raging milk inside that could engulf our research vessel at any moment, we would almost wish to treat this place as the perfect refuge to welcome the end of the world. We really couldn’t be sure whether this was merely an accident or a new idea she’d come up with to tease the mortal world using her divine power. Fortunately, we’re small enough right now that she hasn’t spotted us yet.  nBack in the main world, we broached the subject with [event_target:gts_random_storm_leader_target.GetName] in a roundabout way. She seemed quite surprised—perhaps she hadn’t expected that she could destroy the galaxy in this manner, forcing countless living beings to submit to her bodily secretions. Let’s hope this experience doesn’t awaken any unsavory interests in her. \nAt least she’s been cooperative. The administrative department will dispatch a large number of personnel and machines into her mammary glands to install water level monitoring and storage devices, in order to prevent more milk from flooding into the Milky Way uncontrollably. She will also limit her outings during this period, quietly waiting for the storm she created to subside. The Public Relations Department will also impose news restrictions to prevent the spread of statements such as “[event_target:gts_random_storm_leader_target.GetName] extinguishes stars with her milk,” which, though factually accurate, would damage her personal image. \nOur scientists predict that this rift is unstable and will close completely within a few months to a few years. However, the sweat storm that has already been poured into the Milky Way through the portal can only be left to time to resolve."
