e spaceships and satellites swept into the spatial fissures into fragments, which then stick to her feet, becoming imperceptible adornments. We really can’t be sure if this was just an accident or a new way for her to use her divine power to play tricks on the mortal world. Fortunately, we’re small enough right now that she hasn’t spotted us yet.  nBack in the main world, we broached the subject with [event_target:gts_random_storm_leader_target.GetName] in a roundabout way. She seemed quite surprised—perhaps she hadn’t expected to be able to destroy the galaxy in this manner, forcing countless living beings to cower beneath her bodily secretions. Let’s hope this experience doesn’t awaken any unsavory hobbies in her.\nAt least she’s cooperating with the investigation. The administrative department will dispatch a large number of mechanical units to enter her socks and thoroughly clean the crevices between the cotton socks to ensure proper ventilation. She will also reduce her outdoor activities during this time, quietly waiting for the storm she created to subside. The Public Relations Department will also impose news restrictions to prevent the spread of statements such as “[event_target:gts_random_storm_leader_target.GetName] extinguishes stars with her jade-like feet clad in white silk stockings”—statements that, while factual, would damage her personal image. \nOur scientists predict that this fissure is unstable and will close completely within a few months to a few years. However, the sweat storm that has already poured into the Milky Way through the portal can only be left to time to resolve."
